WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:03.679
If you want to know more about Jigsaw’s
backstory like the details only included in

00:00:03.679 --> 00:00:07.430
the comic, and if you want to see the full
chronology of what I think is the only accurate

00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:11.220
timeline of the events of John Kramer’s
life on the internet, then stick around to

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:14.599
the end of this video.

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:20.850
Many of my favorite horror villains are not
monsters in the typical sense of having a

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:24.930
scary appearance or intimidating demeanor,
but instead project more of a psychological

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:28.410
horror, oftentimes brought on by a distorted
sense of how they see the world.

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:32.050
Many of the best antagonists or anti-heroes
are scary to me because they actually believe

00:00:32.050 --> 00:00:35.580
that they are doing the world a service with
their misdeeds, and the agent of the events

00:00:35.580 --> 00:00:40.290
we’ve come to know as The Saw Franchise
is a model example of this chilling behaviour.

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:42.670
Welcome to Horror History my name is Very
****ing Confused.

00:00:42.670 --> 00:00:46.059
“My name is very ****ing confused, what’s
your name?”

00:00:46.059 --> 00:00:49.830
And in today’s lesson I’ll be analysing
the man responsible for years of citywide

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:54.470
panic, a slew of impersonators, a cult of
nefarious followers, a massive federal investigation

00:00:54.470 --> 00:00:57.490
and most significantly the deaths of at least
57 victims.

00:00:57.490 --> 00:01:02.899
I am of course referring to The Jigsaw Killer,
John Kramer, most commonly known by the nickname:

00:01:02.899 --> 00:01:06.729
Jigsaw, which was originally derived from
his practice of cutting Jigsaw pieces from

00:01:06.729 --> 00:01:11.170
the flesh of his failed victims as a symbol
for the missing piece of their survival instinct.

00:01:11.170 --> 00:01:14.860
In this video we’re going to look at Jigsaw’s
entire life to put together those pieces,

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:18.869
and as with any puzzle, the best way to start
is by figuring out the adjacent pieces, the

00:01:18.869 --> 00:01:23.850
corner pieces such as John Kramer’s past. We'll also explore
the mysteries of his background, the development

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:28.100
of his psychopathy, the imposition of a God-complex
with the religious parallels in his work,

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:31.259
and finally, the realization of his ultimate
failure.

00:01:31.259 --> 00:01:35.229
So in order to understand how the puzzle that
is John Kramer was built, let’s take it

00:01:35.229 --> 00:01:37.530
all the way back to his birth.

00:01:41.032 --> 00:01:44.869
John Kramer was born in the year 1954, a fact
we are able to derive from the mention of

00:01:44.869 --> 00:01:45.869
his age at the time of death.

00:01:45.869 --> 00:01:48.385
“Subject’s name is John Kramer.

00:01:48.385 --> 00:01:50.961
A 52 year old male caucasian.

00:01:50.971 --> 00:01:53.914
So he was only in his early 50s during the
Saw movies?

00:01:53.914 --> 00:01:54.914
YIKES.

00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.719
With a capital YIKES.

00:01:56.719 --> 00:01:57.969
Like the whole thing is capital.

00:01:57.969 --> 00:02:01.509
John’s work consisted of a company he founded
called The Urban Renewal Group, but despite

00:02:01.509 --> 00:02:04.249
how it sounds, this had nothing to do with
mid-2000s hip-hop.

00:02:04.249 --> 00:02:07.959
John was a civil engineer who worked alongside
a lawyer named Art Blank to build homes for

00:02:07.959 --> 00:02:11.720
low-income families and also sometimes created
other buildings with the intent of helping

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:12.720
people.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:16.090
John was extremely intelligent, making him
a world class engineer, but he was also great

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:19.939
at understanding people and anticipating their
actions, which made him quite successful on

00:02:19.939 --> 00:02:21.070
the business end as well.

00:02:21.070 --> 00:02:24.469
He was quickly able to scale Urban Renewal
Group to the point that he owned several buildings

00:02:24.469 --> 00:02:27.989
throughout the city and had a fair amount
of resources, which he channelled back into

00:02:27.989 --> 00:02:29.610
helping the people of that city.

00:02:29.610 --> 00:02:33.829
The desire to help improve people’s lives
was the first key moment to understand his

00:02:33.829 --> 00:02:36.819
motivation, because it was this that drove
his actions throughout his entire life.

00:02:36.819 --> 00:02:39.970
I would also speculate that it was the reason
he fell in love with the woman that would

00:02:39.970 --> 00:02:43.819
become his wife, Jill Tuck, the doctor who
ran a recovery center for drug addicts known

00:02:43.819 --> 00:02:44.989
as Homeward Bound Clinic.

00:02:44.989 --> 00:02:48.590
The clinic’s motto was “cherish your life”
a phrase that John would also associate with

00:02:48.590 --> 00:02:49.590
his own work.

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:53.000
John and Jill’s love eventually led to marriage
and plans to have a first child.

00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:57.000
Like in his work, John meticulously planned
all aspects of his life and the baby was no

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:58.000
exception.

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.219
The child’s name, Gideon, was also the name
of his first building, The Gideon Meatpacking

00:03:01.219 --> 00:03:05.190
Plant and may have been drawn from the Hebrew
name Gidon, which meant hero or judge, showing

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:08.209
us John’s subconscious desire to judge people
for their sins.

00:03:08.209 --> 00:03:12.159
The baby’s planned date of birth was in
1995, the Chinese Year of the Pig, which was

00:03:12.159 --> 00:03:14.930
a symbol of rebirth, a concept that John believed
heavily in.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:18.599
The name Gideon and the pig symbol would have
greater meaning later in John’s story, but

00:03:18.599 --> 00:03:21.090
for now, he was focused on tending to his
pregnant wife.

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:24.459
He would wait for her to get done with work
some days, and he noticed some shady characters

00:03:24.459 --> 00:03:26.069
who were patients at the clinic.

00:03:26.069 --> 00:03:29.540
One evening he has to intervene when a fight
nearly breaks out between two addicts named

00:03:29.540 --> 00:03:33.549
Cecil Adams and Gus Colyard, and John has
to convince Cecil to put his knife away before

00:03:33.549 --> 00:03:34.930
things get much worse.

00:03:34.930 --> 00:03:39.000
This causes John to wonder how effective his
wife’s rehabilitation methods really are,

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.719
but he still encourages her work, something
he would come to regret later down the line.

00:03:42.719 --> 00:03:45.780
He also displays evidence that he’s become
more jaded towards the world when he meets

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:49.269
an insurance mogul named William Easton, who
sponsors a party at Jill’s clinic.

00:03:49.269 --> 00:03:53.120
They seem to connect over their mutual need
to predict human behaviour in their respective

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.749
jobs, but John disagrees with William’s
methods of trying to screen people and determine

00:03:56.749 --> 00:03:59.430
their probability of illness before giving
them insurance coverage.

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:03.120
“But you’re not taking into consideration
the most important human element of all.”

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:04.279
“Which is what?”

00:04:04.279 --> 00:04:05.829
“The will to live.”

00:04:05.829 --> 00:04:09.750
This exchange would be another important puzzle
piece in the crafting of the Jigsaw persona,

00:04:09.750 --> 00:04:13.049
because John believed that he was giving each
of his victims a chance to survive by putting

00:04:13.049 --> 00:04:14.079
them through adversity.

00:04:14.079 --> 00:04:17.430
As Gideon’s due date got closer though,
John continued to prepare for the birth of

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:21.419
his son by constructing a crib, a children’s
toy that resembled a ventriloquist doll, which

00:04:21.419 --> 00:04:25.520
he would name Billy the Puppet and by creating
a home video for the boy during an ultrasound

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:26.520
monitoring.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.599
Again, we can pull a couple of puzzle pieces
from John’s preparation to be a father.

00:04:29.599 --> 00:04:33.030
The messages he meant to save for his son
were to be passed via video tape, and he would

00:04:33.030 --> 00:04:36.320
eventually use this this medium to speak to
his test subjects, while the puppet would

00:04:36.320 --> 00:04:40.050
be reimagined as the face of Jigsaw, an avatar
that appeared in some of the tapes and who

00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:43.520
would sometimes make physical appearances
to carry on messages to his victims.

00:04:43.520 --> 00:04:44.889
[Billy the Puppet laughter]

00:04:44.889 --> 00:04:46.940
“No, that’s not creepy at all.”

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:51.150
Unfortunately, before John ever got to meet
his son Gideon, tragedy would strike on one

00:04:51.150 --> 00:04:53.259
fateful night.

00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:11.979
One evening in late 1994, John warms up the
car while his pregnant wife closes up the

00:05:11.979 --> 00:05:15.320
clinic and notices a distressed Cecil Adams
burst out of the building.

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:19.090
He immediately knows something is wrong and
goes in to find Jill collapsed on the floor

00:05:19.090 --> 00:05:22.020
after having been hit by the swinging door
when Cecil had broken in.

00:05:22.020 --> 00:05:25.669
Jill was 7 months pregnant at this point,
so fearing for the baby’s safety, he rushes

00:05:25.669 --> 00:05:26.740
her to a hospital.

00:05:26.740 --> 00:05:31.250
John suffers a long evening of emotional suffering,
and Jill is shell shocked after doctors are

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:32.780
unable to save the baby.

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:37.060
This is the beginning of John’s descent,
his downward spiral, if you will, into becoming

00:05:37.060 --> 00:05:38.099
a psychopath.

00:05:38.099 --> 00:05:41.750
The most common characteristic of a psycho
is lack of empathy for their victims or remorse

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:45.620
for their actions, and we see the very beginning
of this right after the loss of Gideon, when

00:05:45.620 --> 00:05:48.990
John changes his attitude towards the drug
addicts that he previously encouraged the

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:50.139
idea of helping.

00:05:51.717 --> 00:05:55.379
“All I wanted to do was help them.”

00:05:55.379 --> 00:05:58.000
“You can’t help them.

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:01.280
They have to help themselves.”

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:05.289
Trauma induced psychopathy is one of the three
major ways known to develop the condition,

00:06:05.289 --> 00:06:09.430
and for John, losing the son he had already
committed so much devotion to was the distressing

00:06:09.430 --> 00:06:11.289
catalyst that set things into motion.

00:06:11.289 --> 00:06:14.740
We see how much it affected him by the fact
that he buried Gideon and marked the spot

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:18.120
with a tombstone, a practice not normally
used for a miscarriage.

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:21.690
Even those closest to him, like his wife and
his business partner were not in contact with

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:22.699
him, which worried them.

00:06:22.699 --> 00:06:26.110
They decided to get together to confront him,
and find him sleeping in a chair at his workshop

00:06:26.110 --> 00:06:27.639
in Gideon Meat Packing Plant.

00:06:27.639 --> 00:06:31.370
He's very unwelcoming towards them, showing
no desire to return to his normal life.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:35.090
Art encourages him to channel his negative
energy into their Urban Renewal Project, where

00:06:35.090 --> 00:06:38.569
his designs would have been used to help
low-income families, but he forfeits his shares

00:06:38.569 --> 00:06:41.280
in the company to Jill, and angrily tells
them to get out.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:44.919
He had accomplished many things at this point
in his life, but none of them had been enough

00:06:44.919 --> 00:06:48.889
to save his family from the unpredictable
crimes of a drug addict, and in his depressed

00:06:48.889 --> 00:06:52.110
mindset, he forced himself to come up with
a solution to people like Cecil.

00:06:52.110 --> 00:06:54.500
It was the only way he knew how to cope with
the loss.

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:58.000
He would use the concept of “they have to
help themselves” in his work, and in his

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:01.919
deranged state, he figured the first person
he should give that opportunity to was his

00:07:01.919 --> 00:07:02.919
son’s killer.

00:07:02.919 --> 00:07:06.490
He tracks down Cecil during a celebration
of the Chinese New Year, which, knowing John,

00:07:06.490 --> 00:07:08.470
was likely the planned due date of Gideon.

00:07:08.470 --> 00:07:12.229
To disguise himself, he steals a pig mask,
remember, it was Year of the Pig.

00:07:12.229 --> 00:07:15.400
I’m just glad he upgraded to something a
little bit more spooky later on, because if I

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:18.780
saw my kidnapper wearing this, I’d probably
just start losing it… like what are you

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:19.780
going to do?

00:07:19.780 --> 00:07:22.020
Force me to star in children’s daytime television
programming?

00:07:22.020 --> 00:07:24.110
Actually, that does sound horrifying.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:27.240
But another reason it makes sense for him
to use the pig mask was that the pig in the

00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:31.060
Chinese Zodiac represented rebirth, and he
viewed his games as a chance for victims to

00:07:31.060 --> 00:07:32.539
be reborn as better people.

00:07:32.539 --> 00:07:35.680
He chloroforms Cecil, who next awakens in
John’s workshop.

00:07:35.680 --> 00:07:37.930
“You did this to me.”

00:07:37.930 --> 00:07:40.300
“No, you did this to yourself.”

00:07:40.300 --> 00:07:41.900
Yeah come on Cecil.

00:07:41.900 --> 00:07:42.900
You did this.

00:07:42.900 --> 00:07:44.110
This was all you buddy.

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:45.639
He’s delusional.

00:07:45.639 --> 00:07:47.240
Cecil is trapped in the knife chair.

00:07:47.240 --> 00:07:49.290
John claims it is a tool to reclaim his life.

00:07:49.290 --> 00:07:52.659
If he can press his face through a barrier
of eight knives and press a lever on the other

00:07:52.659 --> 00:07:54.650
side his restraints will be released.

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:58.280
John thinks this is fitting because it will
make Cecil’s face ugly to match his greedy

00:07:58.280 --> 00:07:59.280
soul.

00:07:59.280 --> 00:08:02.099
Cecil is able to release himself from the
chair, but this is not enough to rehabilitate

00:08:02.099 --> 00:08:03.099
him.

00:08:03.099 --> 00:08:06.229
He tries to attack John, who sidesteps and
sends him tumbling into the razor wire trap,

00:08:06.229 --> 00:08:10.230
and this one, he’s unable to escape.

00:08:12.719 --> 00:08:16.229
John may have told himself that letting Cecil
die after giving him a second chance was a

00:08:16.229 --> 00:08:20.669
good thing, that Cecil was unable to be rehabilitated,
and so, killing him was just.

00:08:20.669 --> 00:08:23.849
Another trait of a psychopath is the need
for repeated stimulation.

00:08:23.849 --> 00:08:27.320
Because John felt he was doing Cecil a favor
by putting him through his test, he soon had

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:31.800
the desire to "help" more people and began
to create more complex traps in his workshop.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:36.130
But John's good intentions would not be enough
to make future traps fair or just, and before

00:08:36.130 --> 00:08:39.590
long, police would recognize Kramer's actions
as the work of a serial killer.

00:08:39.590 --> 00:08:41.920
GORDON: "Newspapers started calling him The Jigsaw Killer."

00:08:41.920 --> 00:08:45.470
Hoping to do something about the decline of
her marriage after losing the baby she was

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:48.880
carrying, Jill decided to try to talk to John
and give him one more chance, so she goes

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:50.290
back into the workshop.

00:08:50.290 --> 00:08:53.480
Before finding her husband, she discovers
reconnaissance photos of Cecil Adams.

00:08:53.480 --> 00:08:57.440
Cecil was believed to be missing, and Jill
wondered if John had anything to do with it.

00:08:57.440 --> 00:09:01.610
He finds her snooping around and becomes very
angry with her, telling her not to ever come

00:09:01.610 --> 00:09:05.770
back, effectively the end of their relationship,
and another sign of psychopathic behavior,

00:09:05.770 --> 00:09:06.770
impulsivity.

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:08.420
They would get divorced not long after.

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:11.690
After Jill leaves, he goes back to work on
another trap, the glass coffin.

00:09:11.690 --> 00:09:15.830
This box would allow the user to be transported
out of a collapsing room and brought to safety.

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:18.060
John wouldn't survive long enough to use this
himself.

00:09:18.060 --> 00:09:21.690
Instead, it would be used years later by his
successor, but the fact that he was working

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:25.710
on it way back in the 90s is a testament to
John's intelligence and ability to predict

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:29.710
possible outcomes, one of the things that
makes him so dangerous as a serial killer.

00:09:29.710 --> 00:09:33.270
Despite his impressive intellect, his physical
condition was about to worsen, as John was

00:09:33.270 --> 00:09:37.160
diagnosed with colon cancer not long after
the divorce.

00:09:45.000 --> 00:09:48.870
Between the divorce and the cancer diagnosis,
this was two straight tragedies for John.

00:09:48.870 --> 00:09:52.420
The cancer got to him while he was already
at the lowest of low points, and as a result,

00:09:52.420 --> 00:09:54.100
he decided to end his life.

00:09:54.100 --> 00:09:58.680
He decides to do this Groundhog Day style,
by driving his car off a cliff, but miraculously,

00:09:58.680 --> 00:09:59.840
he survives the wreck.

00:09:59.840 --> 00:10:04.010
As he is lying in the smoking mess, he realizes
that he wants to live, and in order to do

00:10:04.010 --> 00:10:07.850
so, he must endure a little more pain by pulling
a stake out of himself to escape.

00:10:07.850 --> 00:10:11.630
Not only was this a revelation for John in
that he got to experience first hand how testing

00:10:11.630 --> 00:10:15.530
his own will to live had supposedly healed
his mind and given him newfound appreciation

00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:19.450
for life, but it also may have inspired him
directly to create The Spike Trap, a trap

00:10:19.450 --> 00:10:23.170
that would be used years later and required
the a victim to remove metal stakes from herself

00:10:23.170 --> 00:10:27.500
in order to escape; and the Horsepower Trap,
where a victim literally experiences a car

00:10:27.500 --> 00:10:28.000
crash.

00:10:28.000 --> 00:10:30.000
MEME GIRL: "Here's. The motherf"

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:32.000
*Huge Crash*

00:10:32.349 --> 00:10:35.090
🎵 "Don't stop, keep going." 🎵

00:10:35.090 --> 00:10:39.080
After walking away from his self-imposed car
wreck, his faith in the rehabilitation method

00:10:39.080 --> 00:10:42.730
he had tried on Cecil was restored, and he
may have realized that the pain factor would

00:10:42.730 --> 00:10:46.080
need to be amplified, because in order for
it to work, the traps would need to test the

00:10:46.080 --> 00:10:47.820
very fabric of human nature.

00:10:47.820 --> 00:10:51.330
He got to work on some new traps as he was
being treated at the Angel of Mercy Hospital,

00:10:51.330 --> 00:10:55.160
where he ended up being unsatisfied with the
hospitality of almost everyone working there,

00:10:55.160 --> 00:10:57.990
and marked them in his mind as future victims
to be rehabilitated.

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:01.520
The people he encountered there were mostly
just doing their jobs, but because John was

00:11:01.520 --> 00:11:05.520
becoming more frustrated by the tragedies
of his life, he was looking too hard for victims

00:11:05.520 --> 00:11:08.080
to punish by finding reasons that weren't
really there.

00:11:08.080 --> 00:11:11.890
Over the course of the next 5-7 years, John
began to pay more attention to the world around

00:11:11.890 --> 00:11:15.060
him as he continued to receive chemotherapy
for his colon cancer.

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:18.170
He came to meet some of the other people who
he deemed as unappreciative of their lives

00:11:18.170 --> 00:11:20.490
and planned to include them in his upcoming
test game.

00:11:20.490 --> 00:11:24.260
A game, in his eyes, was a series of different
traps involving multiple people, that was

00:11:24.260 --> 00:11:27.900
supposed to add a social experiment element
to his patented rehabilitation process.

00:11:27.900 --> 00:11:29.850
OK, it wasn’t really patented.

00:11:29.850 --> 00:11:32.790
I just thought that word sounded good there
to be honest.

00:11:32.790 --> 00:11:36.530
He had hoped to do more than simply spend
his time testing a series of individuals until

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:38.090
his time on this Earth expired.

00:11:38.090 --> 00:11:42.270
Instead, he wanted to create a long-lasting
societal change that would impact people long

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:46.130
after his passing, by running his games and
letting a survivor go on to tell the tale

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:47.290
of their trial.

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:50.830
When news of the horrors they experienced
broke, others would be less likely to make

00:11:50.830 --> 00:11:53.620
the same mistake out of fear of becoming the
next victim.

00:11:53.620 --> 00:11:57.970
John wanted to turn one random act of supposed
vigilante justice into an entire movement,

00:11:57.970 --> 00:12:00.620
but soon found it could become even more than
that.

00:12:00.620 --> 00:12:04.710
He decided to hold his first game as a test,
and so, created and ran it in secret at a

00:12:04.710 --> 00:12:08.280
remote location, an abandoned pig farm that
was still owned by his wife's family.

00:12:08.280 --> 00:12:12.560
He thought this was the perfect choice because
it fit his idea of the pig icon representing

00:12:12.560 --> 00:12:13.560
rebirth.

00:12:13.560 --> 00:12:16.360
Some of the victims of this test game were
people in his life at the time.

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:19.330
This first game was a bit different than the
others, in that it was more about getting

00:12:19.330 --> 00:12:21.570
the victims to admit the mistakes of their
past.

00:12:21.570 --> 00:12:24.940
The later games were more about putting the
perpetrators in physical pain, which is usually

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:26.560
somehow symbolic of their wrongdoing.

00:12:26.560 --> 00:12:28.940
There would be five players included in the
Barn Game.

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:32.580
There was Ryan, whose foolish actions got
his friends killed back in high school; Carly,

00:12:32.580 --> 00:12:36.740
a thief who caused her victim to have an asthma
attack; Mitch, who sold a faulty motorcycle

00:12:36.740 --> 00:12:40.550
resulting in the death of John's nephew; Anna,
who was John's next door neighbor and was

00:12:40.550 --> 00:12:44.070
normally very supportive of him while going
through chemotherapy, but who also killed

00:12:44.070 --> 00:12:48.580
her baby and blamed it on her sleeping husband
and Logan Nelson, a resident of Angel of Mercy

00:12:48.580 --> 00:12:52.400
Hospital who accidentally switched the labels
of John's brain scan with that if another

00:12:52.400 --> 00:12:55.260
patient, which delayed the diagnosis of a
tumor on John's brain.

00:12:55.260 --> 00:12:59.860
As a result of this, he wasn't correctly diagnosed
until 2003, and by that point it's too late.

00:12:59.860 --> 00:13:04.610
The physicians working on his case, Dr. Lawrence
Gordon and Dr. Lynn Denlon were cold and unsympathetic

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:08.350
to him during his treatment, and John did
not like the way Dr. Gordon told him how long

00:13:08.350 --> 00:13:09.350
he had to live.

00:13:09.350 --> 00:13:12.700
He planned to possibly test the two doctors
in future games, but for now, he had collected

00:13:12.700 --> 00:13:16.410
enough players to run his test game, so he
collected them, brought them to the Tuck Pig

00:13:16.410 --> 00:13:19.120
Farm and John Kramer's first experiment began.

00:13:19.120 --> 00:13:23.460
JIGSAW: "Any attempt to violate my rules will kill
you.

00:13:23.460 --> 00:13:25.370
I want to play a game."

00:13:25.370 --> 00:13:28.670
When the game begins, John keeps track of
the progress of each player by monitoring

00:13:28.670 --> 00:13:30.420
the rooms with security cameras.

00:13:30.420 --> 00:13:33.730
Later iterations of the games would have him
physically present to make sure that the rules

00:13:33.730 --> 00:13:37.130
of each game are followed, so I'm guessing
that technology was used here in the test

00:13:37.130 --> 00:13:42.440
game because two of the contestants, Anna
and Logan, already knew who John Kramer was.

00:13:43.430 --> 00:13:45.770
“Hello Anna.”

00:13:45.770 --> 00:13:47.440
“John?”

00:13:47.440 --> 00:13:50.950
Each player wakes up with a bucket on their
head and is instructed to make a blood sacrifice,

00:13:50.950 --> 00:13:55.120
but Logan didn't wake up at the same time
as the others, giving him an unfair disadvantage.

00:13:55.120 --> 00:13:58.180
John recognises this, and doesn't think it
would be right for Logan to die because of

00:13:58.180 --> 00:14:01.410
a small mistake, so he stops the spinning
saw blades and bails him out.

00:14:01.410 --> 00:14:04.740
Logan had suffered large lacerations across
his back, but with John's help, he's able

00:14:04.740 --> 00:14:06.750
to have them stitched up and he survives.

00:14:06.750 --> 00:14:10.220
From there, the rest of the game plays out
as planned until there are only two survivors

00:14:10.220 --> 00:14:11.920
remaining, Anna and Ryan.

00:14:11.920 --> 00:14:15.521
Wearing the updated version of the pig mask,
John re-enters the game and once more

00:14:15.521 --> 00:14:16.521
sedates them.

00:14:16.521 --> 00:14:19.080
While they are unconscious, he moves them
to another part of the barn called the slaughter

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.080
room.

00:14:20.080 --> 00:14:22.380
If you're wondering if there's a reason it's
called that, there is.

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:24.050
And there's about to be a second one.

00:14:24.050 --> 00:14:27.370
Ryan and Anna are locked to opposite sides
of the room and John finally reveals himself

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:30.160
to deliver the rules of this final challenge.

00:14:30.717 --> 00:14:32.590
JIGSAW: "Now The game is simple.

00:14:32.590 --> 00:14:34.568
The best ones are.

00:14:36.115 --> 00:14:38.354
You have one shotgun.

00:14:39.654 --> 00:14:40.654
You have one shell."

00:14:40.839 --> 00:14:44.050
He doesn’t specifically tell them that the
gun is configured backwards.

00:14:44.050 --> 00:14:47.170
The theme of this game from the beginning
was for them to find salvation by looking

00:14:47.170 --> 00:14:48.170
inwards.

00:14:48.170 --> 00:14:53.480
JIGSAW: "While I am certain that there is a desire to point
fingers at me for the blood that has been

00:14:53.480 --> 00:15:00.830
shed, unless you turn that finger inward,
I assure you more blood will be lost.”

00:15:00.830 --> 00:15:03.030
The same principle ends up applying for the
gun.

00:15:03.030 --> 00:15:07.020
JIGSAW: “Now if you want to achieve your freedom,
you have to learn.

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:11.480
You have to realize that you’ve been doing
it backwards.”

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:15.620
...so when Anna fails to take these clues
into consideration and tries killing Ryan

00:15:15.620 --> 00:15:17.700
with the gun, she ends up shooting herself.

00:15:17.700 --> 00:15:21.130
The key that would have released them was
also hidden in the bullet casing left inside

00:15:21.130 --> 00:15:25.310
the gun, so it is destroyed when Anna shoots
it and so are Ryan's chances of ever escaping.

00:15:25.310 --> 00:15:29.140
That leaves only one survivor of the test
game, Logan Nelson, and he would actually

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:32.900
be the one to give shape to the next piece
of the Jigsaw puzzle.

00:15:40.340 --> 00:15:43.480
Let's just go back just one moment to the point
where John Kramer reveals himself in a game

00:15:43.480 --> 00:15:44.640
for the first time.

00:15:44.640 --> 00:15:48.380
When he comes out to address Ryan and Anna,
he's wearing a new costume, a hooded robe

00:15:48.380 --> 00:15:50.840
that almost makes him look like a monk or
priest.

00:15:50.840 --> 00:15:54.680
This pig farm was no temple, but the attire
does lead me into the next piece of the Jigsaw

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.300
puzzle: the religious aspect of John's teachings.

00:15:57.300 --> 00:16:00.900
When I said he was creating a movement, it's
wasn't only about scaring the citizens into

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:04.540
behaving as he wants them to, based on the
cautionary tales of the survivors; but he

00:16:04.540 --> 00:16:08.170
also wanted to develop his own cult, his own
group of followers that could pass down his

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:10.860
teachings and eventually take over for him
when he was gone.

00:16:10.860 --> 00:16:14.090
In order to truly change the world, he would
have to create something that would still

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:18.350
inspire this behaviour for future generations,
and the only way to do that was for his followers

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:19.835
to pass down his values.

00:16:19.835 --> 00:16:21.663
“Change da world.

00:16:21.663 --> 00:16:24.140
My final message.

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:27.087
Goodbye.”

00:16:33.120 --> 00:16:36.870
The first step to doing this is by painting
himself as a religious leader by wearing these

00:16:36.870 --> 00:16:37.870
robes.

00:16:37.870 --> 00:16:39.760
In doing so, he started to see himself as
a God.

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:43.950
As discussed in the Horror History episode
on Mark Hoffman, a God complex is an unshakable

00:16:43.950 --> 00:16:48.250
belief characterized by consistently inflated
feelings of personal ability, privilege, or

00:16:48.250 --> 00:16:49.250
infallibility.

00:16:49.250 --> 00:16:51.120
In other words, he thinks he can do no wrong.

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:55.270
The religious attire was kind of a final step
towards John truly believing that he was a

00:16:55.270 --> 00:16:59.450
God, and according to psychologist and author
Harold Kaplan's definition of a God-complex,

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:01.411
Jigsaw's behaviour fits to a T.

00:17:01.411 --> 00:17:05.459
"A person with a god complex may refuse to
admit the possibility of their error or failure,

00:17:05.459 --> 00:17:08.589
even in the face of irrefutable evidence and
intractable problems."

00:17:08.589 --> 00:17:12.269
In John's case, look no further than his previous
trap with Cecil Adams.

00:17:12.269 --> 00:17:15.780
He believed that if Cecil suffered through
the knife chair, he would be instantly rehabilitated.

00:17:15.780 --> 00:17:18.990
But he wasn't, he still tried to attack John
after escaping.

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:23.549
But even after seeing that go down, John refuses
to believe his methods are faulty, and continues

00:17:23.549 --> 00:17:25.039
with his plans to create new traps.

00:17:25.039 --> 00:17:28.730
I also think it's no coincidence that Cecil's
surname is 'Adams'.

00:17:28.730 --> 00:17:32.240
Cecil is John's first victim to be punished
for wrongdoing, and in the biblical story

00:17:32.240 --> 00:17:35.940
of Adam and Eve, Adam is the one to take the
forbidden fruit, which gets them banned from

00:17:35.940 --> 00:17:36.970
The Garden of Eden.

00:17:36.970 --> 00:17:42.020
“I’m not really sure how I have to say
this but, I just have to say this so that

00:17:42.020 --> 00:17:44.039
no one makes the same mistake I’ve done.

00:17:44.039 --> 00:17:47.630
I’m not sure how many of you know this but
I’ve actually been permanently banned…

00:17:47.630 --> 00:17:48.630
for life.”

00:17:48.630 --> 00:17:52.179
Other indicators of a God-complex include
"a person highly dogmatic in their views",

00:17:52.179 --> 00:17:55.690
meaning the person speaks of their personal
opinions as though they were unquestionably

00:17:55.690 --> 00:17:56.690
correct.

00:17:56.690 --> 00:17:59.720
Just listen to the way John addresses his
victims, in a booming God-like voice might

00:17:59.720 --> 00:18:02.509
I add, as if his judgements of them are completely
irrefutable.

00:18:02.509 --> 00:18:08.610
“You deny culpability no doubt, for the
circumstances in which you find yourselves,

00:18:08.610 --> 00:18:15.799
salvation can be yours if you cleanse yourselves
of the habitual lies, which have brought you

00:18:15.799 --> 00:18:16.799
here.”

00:18:16.799 --> 00:18:19.960
He even speaks using language that you might
find in religious texts when addressing his

00:18:19.960 --> 00:18:20.960
victims.

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:24.610
The final indicator of a God-complex is exhibiting
“no regard for the conventions and demands

00:18:24.610 --> 00:18:25.610
of society.

00:18:25.610 --> 00:18:28.049
They may request special consideration or
privileges.”

00:18:28.049 --> 00:18:30.419
John’s methods are against the law, obviously.

00:18:30.419 --> 00:18:33.929
He would soon start holding more public facing
games, but since he views what he’s doing

00:18:33.929 --> 00:18:37.120
as morally just, he disregards the rules of
our society.

00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:38.900
OFFICER RIGG: “Get his ass out of here.”

00:18:38.900 --> 00:18:44.309
JIGSAW: “Actually, I will need to remain here while you deal with
your problem, Detective Matthews.”

00:18:44.309 --> 00:18:48.760
So John is a textbook example of someone with
a God-complex, but a religion cannot work

00:18:48.760 --> 00:18:52.929
with only a God or leader, it also requires
followers, and John had already found his

00:18:52.929 --> 00:18:53.929
first one.

00:18:53.929 --> 00:18:57.299
After saving Logan Nelson from the barn game,
he takes him under his wing and trains him

00:18:57.299 --> 00:18:58.440
in the ways of Jigsaw.

00:18:58.440 --> 00:19:01.070
He explains the basic concepts upon which
he operates.

00:19:01.070 --> 00:19:05.350
Many religions use some kind of text or commandments
to impress a moral code on their followers.

00:19:05.350 --> 00:19:08.860
Jigsaw’s games each have rules, and the
ideals expressed in these tapes serve as the

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:11.950
religious texts, the main method of John Kramer’s
teachings.

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:15.659
Most religious texts date back thousands of
years or more, and John’s teachings gain

00:19:15.659 --> 00:19:19.520
a similar immortality when a website is founded
to spread his word even after his death.

00:19:19.520 --> 00:19:23.279
DET. HUNT: “Uh Logan, you ever heard of a website called
Jigsaw rules?”

00:19:23.279 --> 00:19:25.120
DET. HALLORAN: “It’s a site devoted to Jigsaw.”

00:19:25.120 --> 00:19:29.060
And of course, the most important part of
The Cult of Jigsaw, and the Saw franchise

00:19:29.060 --> 00:19:30.650
in general, is the traps.

00:19:30.650 --> 00:19:34.510
In religion, there are usually abstract concepts
of sin leading to punishment.

00:19:34.510 --> 00:19:38.650
Popular ones include heaven and hell, while
others use a system of karma and reincarnation.

00:19:38.650 --> 00:19:41.020
John’s religion kind of combines both ideas.

00:19:41.020 --> 00:19:44.910
The traps cause suffering, as a form of punishment
for those who have sinned, but he views this

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:46.549
suffering as transformative.

00:19:46.549 --> 00:19:49.380
He thinks the survivors of his traps are reborn
as better people.

00:19:49.380 --> 00:19:53.720
And leads us back to Logan Nelson, who would
become the first disciple of Jigsaw.

00:19:53.720 --> 00:19:57.060
John taught him everything he believed in,
and also shared some of his knowledge in the

00:19:57.060 --> 00:19:58.460
field of mechanical engineering.

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:02.190
Together, they created what would become Jigsaw’s
signature trap: The Reverse Bear Trap.

00:20:02.190 --> 00:20:05.809
The partnership would be short lived however,
because Nelson had to go overseas to fight

00:20:05.809 --> 00:20:09.440
in the war, so John would have to look elsewhere
to find more potential disciples.

00:20:09.440 --> 00:20:13.090
As he is still working to fight off the cancer,
he discovers someone who he thinks could potentially

00:20:13.090 --> 00:20:14.820
have what it takes to be one of his followers.

00:20:14.820 --> 00:20:18.940
It all begins when John is doing some of his
own research on alternate treatments, and

00:20:18.940 --> 00:20:22.080
discovers a doctor in Norway who has been
administering an experimental therapy with

00:20:22.080 --> 00:20:24.010
a 30 to 40% success rate.

00:20:24.010 --> 00:20:27.690
He goes to visit his health care provider
Umbrella Health, which is run by William Easton,

00:20:27.690 --> 00:20:29.929
the man who had once sponsored the party at
Jill’s clinic.

00:20:29.929 --> 00:20:33.750
He explains the situation and requests coverage,
but William gives him this copy and paste

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:37.570
answer about how his doctor would already
be using the treatment if it worked, how it’s

00:20:37.570 --> 00:20:41.330
not feasible with John’s insurance policy
and that if he seeks this treatment out independently,

00:20:41.330 --> 00:20:43.460
he’ll be dropped from his current coverage.

00:20:43.460 --> 00:20:46.720
John responds with one of my favorite lines,
that I always make sure to quote if I ever

00:20:46.720 --> 00:20:47.740
have to go to the doctor.

00:20:47.740 --> 00:20:50.990
Whenever it’s time to pay, the receptionist
will just be like, “ok CZsWorld, that’s

00:20:50.990 --> 00:20:54.590
$50,000” and then I just do my best John
Kramer voice and say, “You know, in the

00:20:54.590 --> 00:20:57.490
far east, people pay their doctors when they’re
healthy.”

00:20:57.490 --> 00:20:58.490
And then she’s like, “what?”

00:20:58.490 --> 00:21:01.860
And I say, “You think it’s the living
that will have ultimate judgement over you...”

00:21:01.860 --> 00:21:06.509
No, but I think the reason John reacts the
way he does to Mr. Easton is more out of principle,

00:21:06.509 --> 00:21:09.610
to make a point about the healthcare system
rather than for personal reasons.

00:21:09.610 --> 00:21:13.070
I think he knew he was going to die before
long, and he had the money to seek out other

00:21:13.070 --> 00:21:16.581
treatments, but he wanted his legacy to say
something about society, which is again, something

00:21:16.581 --> 00:21:18.600
that a religious icon might do.

00:21:18.600 --> 00:21:21.649
Later that year, things would get worse with
his health once again, and it was time to

00:21:21.649 --> 00:21:24.010
unleash the Jigsaw icon out into the world.

00:21:24.010 --> 00:21:27.669
The public was about to learn of Jigsaw for
the first time.

00:21:34.034 --> 00:21:39.909
In June of 2003, Dr. Lawrence Gordon diagnosed
John with an Inoperable Frontal Lobe Tumor,

00:21:39.909 --> 00:21:42.639
or Glioblastoma Multiforme of the left temporal
lobe.

00:21:42.639 --> 00:21:45.340
In other words, he had a very fast spreading
brain cancer.

00:21:45.340 --> 00:21:49.490
He underwent chemotherapy to try to kill the
cancer cells and external beam radiation therapy

00:21:49.490 --> 00:21:50.950
to try and remove the tumor.

00:21:50.950 --> 00:21:55.370
Nine months later, on March 24th 2004, John
was found to have progressive aphasia and

00:21:55.370 --> 00:21:56.590
right-sided hemiplegia.

00:21:56.590 --> 00:21:59.990
That means the brain cancer was affecting
his ability to speak, and also limiting his

00:21:59.990 --> 00:22:01.809
ability to move the right side of his body.

00:22:01.809 --> 00:22:04.460
See, we’re learning science as well here
in the Horror History classroom.

00:22:04.460 --> 00:22:06.179
This show is educational guys.

00:22:06.179 --> 00:22:07.259
It’s not just memes.

00:22:07.259 --> 00:22:08.499
It’s not just memes.

00:22:08.499 --> 00:22:09.767
*building laughter and chest opening music*

00:22:09.832 --> 00:22:10.656
"Wait till you see the...

00:22:10.656 --> 00:22:11.821
*building laughter and chest opening music*

00:22:11.821 --> 00:22:13.387
"Oh no, no, no, no!"

00:22:13.387 --> 00:22:16.315
*building laughter and chest opening music*

00:22:16.586 --> 00:22:18.586
*EXPLOSION OF SQUEALING LAUGHTER*

00:22:18.709 --> 00:22:21.499
OK fine, but my point is, it’s not all memes.

00:22:21.499 --> 00:22:25.539
John was examined again and Dr. Gordon and
Dr. Denlon discovered a mass on his left temporal

00:22:25.539 --> 00:22:27.659
lobe causing his brainstem to compress.

00:22:27.659 --> 00:22:30.850
The cancer was also Metastatic, meaning it
was moving to different parts of the brain

00:22:30.850 --> 00:22:32.720
or possibly different parts of the body.

00:22:32.720 --> 00:22:36.850
A further brain scan indicated signs of necrosis;
his brain cells were going to die as a side

00:22:36.850 --> 00:22:40.090
effect of the radiation therapy which was
meant to kill the cancer cells, but didn’t

00:22:40.090 --> 00:22:42.610
necessarily distinguish between good and bad
cells.

00:22:42.610 --> 00:22:46.669
In addition to that, he exhibited edema, so
his brain was swelling inside of his skull,

00:22:46.669 --> 00:22:50.530
forcing them to perform a craniotomy, a brain
surgery that requires them to create a surgical

00:22:50.530 --> 00:22:51.749
opening through his skull.

00:22:51.749 --> 00:22:54.850
If you weren’t paying attention through
most of that medical jargon, basically all

00:22:54.850 --> 00:22:58.820
you need to know is ya boy was sick, and Dr.
Denlon told him, “there’s no preventative

00:22:58.820 --> 00:23:01.850
treatment for what you have”, in a very
cold clinical tone.

00:23:01.850 --> 00:23:03.929
John didn’t appreciate that a whole lot.

00:23:03.929 --> 00:23:07.440
His brain may have had a recurring tumor,
but it didn’t seem to affect his memory,

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:11.340
as he would file Dr. Denlon’s lack of empathy
away in his mind to make her another possible

00:23:11.340 --> 00:23:12.789
test subject in the future.

00:23:12.789 --> 00:23:16.270
In the meantime however, Dr. Gordon and Dr.
Denlon were able to improve his condition

00:23:16.270 --> 00:23:19.750
enough so that he could be released from the
hospital to enjoy what time he had left at

00:23:19.750 --> 00:23:20.750
home.

00:23:20.750 --> 00:23:23.760
However he had other ideas of how he wanted
to spend his precious hours.

00:23:23.760 --> 00:23:27.779
Ironically, we don’t actually see his first
public victims, even though this area in between

00:23:27.779 --> 00:23:31.659
March 2004 and October 2004 has been covered
to death in the movies.

00:23:31.659 --> 00:23:34.529
But basically what we do know is that there
were at least three-or-so traps that were held

00:23:34.529 --> 00:23:36.110
in which none of the victims made it.

00:23:36.110 --> 00:23:39.490
The reason I think this is because the next
death that we do see is the death of Seth

00:23:39.490 --> 00:23:43.330
Baxter in the Pendulum Trap, which was created
by Detective Mark Hoffman to make it look

00:23:43.330 --> 00:23:45.360
like Seth was another victim of Jigsaw.

00:23:45.360 --> 00:23:49.129
But in order for this copycat crime to make
sense, that means there had to have been other

00:23:49.129 --> 00:23:52.299
Jigsaw traps that were discovered by the public
in the first place.

00:23:52.299 --> 00:23:55.730
Even though we don’t see them on this list
of Jigsaw victims in Saw 5.

00:23:55.730 --> 00:23:58.880
Maybe there’s another page to this list
that we don’t see, or maybe they were all

00:23:58.880 --> 00:24:01.540
so badly mutilated that they could not be
identified.

00:24:01.540 --> 00:24:04.990
It certainly wasn’t because the creators
of this franchise are human, and a mistake

00:24:04.990 --> 00:24:05.990
was made.

00:24:05.990 --> 00:24:09.320
In these first three public victims, a few
conventions are established, like the use

00:24:09.320 --> 00:24:12.619
of a pre-recorded tape featuring Billy the
Puppet reading the rules of each trap out

00:24:12.619 --> 00:24:16.190
to the victim, the idea that John is physically
present at the site of each test, and the

00:24:16.190 --> 00:24:19.500
fact that a jigsaw puzzle piece is cut out of the
flesh of each subject.

00:24:19.500 --> 00:24:23.159
As a result of this, the police and the press
coined the name Jigsaw and John became known

00:24:23.159 --> 00:24:24.159
as The Jigsaw Killer.

00:24:24.159 --> 00:24:25.159
“My name’s John.”

00:24:25.159 --> 00:24:27.679
“I thought you liked to be called Jigsaw.”

00:24:27.679 --> 00:24:33.463
“It was the police and the press who coined
the nickname Jigsaw. I never encouraged or claimed that.

00:24:33.463 --> 00:24:39.269
The Jigsaw piece I cut from my subjects was
only ever meant to be a symbol that that subject

00:24:39.269 --> 00:24:40.649
was missing something.”

00:24:40.649 --> 00:24:44.760
Mark Hoffman used these elements in his copycat
Jigsaw trap, but John had already been keeping

00:24:44.760 --> 00:24:48.389
an eye on him for other reasons, so he found
out immediately, and decided to test him as

00:24:48.389 --> 00:24:52.340
well in a crude trap called the shotgun chair,
which prevented Hoffman from moving his arms

00:24:52.340 --> 00:24:54.779
if he didn’t want to… you know… blow
his head off.

00:24:54.779 --> 00:24:58.700
The reason Hoffman is tested is that he didn’t
give his subject a second chance.

00:24:58.700 --> 00:25:00.190
“EVERYBODY DESERVES A CHANCE!”

00:25:00.190 --> 00:25:01.890
...And you get a chance!

00:25:01.890 --> 00:25:05.591
And you get a chance! Hoffman is gonna get
one too, because John realizes that the two

00:25:05.591 --> 00:25:07.950
of them are not too far apart in their intentions.

00:25:07.950 --> 00:25:11.429
They both want to bring justice to the city,
but John believes he has a better way of going

00:25:11.429 --> 00:25:12.960
about it because of his God-complex.

00:25:12.960 --> 00:25:15.460
So he brings Hoffman on as his next disciple.

00:25:15.460 --> 00:25:19.549
To make sure he stays in line, John threatens
that the truth about Hoffman being Seth Baxter’s

00:25:19.549 --> 00:25:21.960
killer will automatically be released if anything
happens to him.

00:25:21.960 --> 00:25:25.370
So Hoffman is forced to work under John, and
John hopes that this will help him see the

00:25:25.370 --> 00:25:27.679
light, and starts to agree with John’s methods.

00:25:27.679 --> 00:25:31.010
In order to start this transformation, John
takes Hoffman along as he sets up the next

00:25:31.010 --> 00:25:32.010
two traps.

00:25:32.010 --> 00:25:35.840
The two of them double team a man named Paul
Leahy and leave him in The Razor Wire Maze

00:25:35.840 --> 00:25:36.840
trap.

00:25:36.840 --> 00:25:39.749
Paul was a former addict that John had first
met at Jill’s clinic, and had since turned

00:25:39.749 --> 00:25:41.559
to cutting himself to feed his addiction.

00:25:41.559 --> 00:25:45.270
The maze seems to be an updated version of
Cecil’s second trap, and Paul was required

00:25:45.270 --> 00:25:47.862
to crawl through, thus cutting himself again
to get out.

00:25:47.862 --> 00:25:52.856
JIGSAW: “The irony, is that if you want to die,
you just have to stay where you are.

00:25:52.856 --> 00:25:56.352
But if you want to live, you’ll have to
cut yourself again.”

00:25:56.352 --> 00:26:00.679
The hope was that this more painful punishment
would get Paul to appreciate the life he had,

00:26:00.679 --> 00:26:03.980
but, it was once again in vain, and Paul was
unable to survive.

00:26:03.980 --> 00:26:07.749
The crime scene was "investigated"
by Hoffman, but the deputy coroner

00:26:07.749 --> 00:26:12.029
on the police force, Allison Kerry introduced
two new investigators to the equation, Stephen

00:26:12.029 --> 00:26:13.769
Sing and David Tapp.

00:26:13.769 --> 00:26:17.279
Jigsaw would keep tabs on them from here on
out and later decided to make them future

00:26:17.279 --> 00:26:18.610
Jigsaw victims.

00:26:18.610 --> 00:26:22.000
Before this, I think you could make the argument
at least that everyone he had tested… even

00:26:22.000 --> 00:26:24.390
if you don’t want to say they deserved it,
they were bad people.

00:26:24.390 --> 00:26:26.820
(Not including Nelson, who really didn’t
end up getting tested.)

00:26:26.820 --> 00:26:30.169
But Sing and Tapp only end up on Jigsaw’s
naughty list because they’re trying to bring

00:26:30.169 --> 00:26:31.649
a serial killer to justice.

00:26:31.649 --> 00:26:35.940
This is both the psychopathy and God-complex
inside of John really taking over and skewing

00:26:35.940 --> 00:26:37.549
his perception of reality.

00:26:37.549 --> 00:26:41.369
These two psychological conditions cause him
to invent reasons to punish Sing and Tapp

00:26:41.369 --> 00:26:42.669
so that nobody can stop him.

00:26:42.669 --> 00:26:45.850
He tried to tell himself that they deserved
to be tested because they valued the glory

00:26:45.850 --> 00:26:48.220
of catching Jigsaw over the preservation of
human life.

00:26:48.220 --> 00:26:51.220
But it was really just an excuse to strike
down those who opposed him.

00:26:51.220 --> 00:26:55.210
So the God-complex told him that nobody should
threaten his power, but his psychopathy told

00:26:55.210 --> 00:26:59.029
him he was doing the right thing by putting
them through nearly inescapable tests.

00:26:59.029 --> 00:27:02.700
John set up a new workshop in an abandoned
mannequin factory on Stygian Street.

00:27:02.700 --> 00:27:06.220
There, he would work on the creation of his
next major game, The Bathroom Game, and he

00:27:06.220 --> 00:27:08.929
would create a trap for Sing and Tapp, so
that they would be killed if they tried to

00:27:08.929 --> 00:27:10.169
confront or stop him.

00:27:10.169 --> 00:27:13.889
He does this by filming the video tapes he
plays for his victims in front of recognizable

00:27:13.889 --> 00:27:18.029
graffiti to lure the two cops into his territory,
but they would not show up there for at least

00:27:18.029 --> 00:27:19.029
a few weeks.

00:27:19.029 --> 00:27:22.249
In the meantime, he had another subject to
test, and once again enlisted the help of

00:27:22.249 --> 00:27:23.249
Hoffman.

00:27:23.249 --> 00:27:24.480
The victim was named Mark Wilson.

00:27:24.480 --> 00:27:27.850
John had found out that Mark was faking an
illness in order to scam others, so he tests

00:27:27.850 --> 00:27:29.809
him using the Flammable Jelly Trap.

00:27:29.809 --> 00:27:33.090
Mark needed to obtain the combination to a
safe containing an antidote, by using a candle

00:27:33.090 --> 00:27:34.929
to read the clues written on the walls.

00:27:34.929 --> 00:27:38.149
The floor was covered in sharp glass, and
one wrong move would ignite the flammable

00:27:38.149 --> 00:27:39.700
jelly smeared over his body.

00:27:39.700 --> 00:27:40.700
That!

00:27:40.700 --> 00:27:42.509
Is why it’s called: The Flammable Jelly
Trap.

00:27:42.509 --> 00:27:46.369
After setting this trap up, Hoffman tries
to warn John that Tapp is onto him, but John,

00:27:46.369 --> 00:27:53.950
the manipulative mastermind that he is, is
already one step ahead of him.

00:27:57.889 --> 00:28:01.440
One day during his treatment at the Angel
of Mercy Hospital, John steals a penlight

00:28:01.440 --> 00:28:05.309
from his oncologist, Dr. Gordon, and passes
it on to Hoffman, instructing him to leave

00:28:05.309 --> 00:28:09.510
it behind at the Flammable Jelly Trap crime
scene in order to throw the other investigators

00:28:09.510 --> 00:28:10.510
off.

00:28:10.510 --> 00:28:13.330
The plan worked, and it gave John a little
bit more freedom when it came to his next

00:28:13.330 --> 00:28:16.559
trap, which would involve two more former
patients of the Homeward Bound Clinic.

00:28:16.559 --> 00:28:20.244
This trap would take place in May of 2004,
five months before the events of the bathroom

00:28:20.244 --> 00:28:20.961
game.

00:28:20.961 --> 00:28:22.461
GORDON: “That was five months ago.”

00:28:22.461 --> 00:28:25.919
And the players this time were two drug addicts
named Amanda Young and Donnie Greco.

00:28:25.919 --> 00:28:29.940
This is another example of Jigsaw believing
his judgements are supreme, but in reality,

00:28:29.940 --> 00:28:31.780
the scenario he creates is unfair.

00:28:31.780 --> 00:28:35.169
Amanda is told she must retrieve the key from
the stomach of her dead cellmate in order

00:28:35.169 --> 00:28:38.460
to remove the reverse bear trap and prevent
it from tearing open her head.

00:28:38.460 --> 00:28:43.089
However, when she begins she finds that Donnie
is not actually dead, just asleep, but she

00:28:43.089 --> 00:28:44.320
has to kill him to get the key.

00:28:44.320 --> 00:28:47.369
We’re not even at the start of the first
movie yet, and John’s already breaking his

00:28:47.369 --> 00:28:48.369
own rules.

00:28:48.369 --> 00:28:50.549
And very loudly yelled ones at that.

00:28:50.549 --> 00:28:52.119
“EVERYBODY DESERVES A CHANCE!”

00:28:52.119 --> 00:28:56.080
As I discussed in my Saw episode of Things
You Missed, it is possible that Donnie already

00:28:56.080 --> 00:28:59.559
had a second chance in a trap of his own,
offscreen somewhere, but what’s most likely

00:28:59.559 --> 00:29:03.059
happening here, is that Jigsaw has developed
a bit of a taste for violence through his

00:29:03.059 --> 00:29:04.059
previous victims.

00:29:04.059 --> 00:29:07.110
It’s another trait of the psychopath, the
need for stimulation.

00:29:07.110 --> 00:29:11.249
Ironically, this makes him no better than
the addicts that he’s so keen on punishing,

00:29:11.249 --> 00:29:15.028
because they’re addicted to drugs and he’s
essentially addicted to putting people in traps.

00:29:15.028 --> 00:29:19.150
He’s made himself the judge, jury and executioner,
and he’s begun to take joy in the power

00:29:19.150 --> 00:29:20.309
that this gives him.

00:29:20.309 --> 00:29:23.830
What makes this even more dangerous is that
fact that he’s super intelligent, and knows

00:29:23.830 --> 00:29:26.809
that he has to be sneaky about what he’s
doing in order for it to continue.

00:29:26.809 --> 00:29:29.926
At this point, Jigsaw is already a full-fledged
monster.

00:29:29.926 --> 00:29:33.595
After Amanda unlocks the reverse bear trap
from her head, Billy the Puppet wheels up

00:29:33.595 --> 00:29:35.750
on a tricycle and congratulates her.

00:29:35.750 --> 00:29:36.750
JIGSAW'S VOICE: “Congratulations.

00:29:36.750 --> 00:29:38.399
You are still alive.

00:29:38.399 --> 00:29:42.659
Most people are so ungrateful to be alive.

00:29:42.659 --> 00:29:44.250
But not you.

00:29:44.250 --> 00:29:45.320
Not anymore.”

00:29:45.320 --> 00:29:48.679
John waits in her apartment for her to get
home and tells her not to be afraid, because

00:29:48.679 --> 00:29:50.049
her life has just begun.

00:29:50.049 --> 00:29:52.129
Amanda would be his next disciple.

00:29:52.129 --> 00:29:55.629
She was the first survivor of a game to actually
believe that the experience had helped her

00:29:55.629 --> 00:29:59.519
overcome something, and felt that her days
of taking drugs were behind her now that she came

00:29:59.519 --> 00:30:00.749
to appreciate life.

00:30:00.749 --> 00:30:04.470
For this reason, John saw great potential
in her to be the one to continue his work,

00:30:04.470 --> 00:30:07.940
so he began to work with her more closely
as he developed his next game, hoping to hone

00:30:07.940 --> 00:30:10.000
her skills and get her up to speed with Hoffman.

00:30:10.000 --> 00:30:14.149
Two weeks later in mid-to-late-May, John predicts
that Sing and Tapp are close to discovering

00:30:14.149 --> 00:30:15.149
his workshop.

00:30:15.149 --> 00:30:18.521
He may have known this because of his excellent
ability to anticipate the actions of others,

00:30:18.521 --> 00:30:22.059
but may have also been aided by Hoffman, who
was still a police officer and may have been

00:30:22.059 --> 00:30:25.490
looking over Tapp’s shoulder to warn John
about when he was getting close.

00:30:25.490 --> 00:30:29.210
He starts wearing a bulletproof vest around
under his robes as a precaution, and kidnaps

00:30:29.210 --> 00:30:31.039
a man named Jeff Ridenhour.

00:30:31.039 --> 00:30:35.100
The reason that Jigsaw wanted to test Jeff
is unknown, because his tape is never discovered,

00:30:35.100 --> 00:30:39.059
however, if we use the non-canon video game
Saw II: Flesh and Blood as clue, it would

00:30:39.059 --> 00:30:43.110
seem that Jeff had attempted suicide, and
thus, John felt he did not cherish his life.

00:30:43.110 --> 00:30:46.929
He imprisons Jeff in a trap known as The Drill
Chair, and waits for Sing and Tapp to find

00:30:46.929 --> 00:30:47.929
him.

00:30:47.929 --> 00:30:50.769
One day when he walks into his workshop, he
realizes that someone has been there, and

00:30:50.769 --> 00:30:52.320
prepares for a confrontation.

00:30:52.320 --> 00:30:54.929
He starts The Drill Chair by stepping on a
switch on the ground, and explains

00:30:54.929 --> 00:30:58.309
that it will kill Jeff in 20 seconds if the
detectives can’t find the key.

00:30:58.309 --> 00:31:01.980
So basically, they have to choose between saving
his life and capturing Jigsaw.

00:31:01.980 --> 00:31:05.049
This is another example of him bending his
own rules to benefit himself.

00:31:05.049 --> 00:31:08.649
Unless there’s some offscreen scene with
Jeff failing his first test, he’s not really

00:31:08.649 --> 00:31:09.950
being given a second chance.

00:31:09.950 --> 00:31:11.960
“EVERYBODY DESERVES A CHANCE!”

00:31:11.960 --> 00:31:14.139
He also claims that he despises murder.

00:31:14.139 --> 00:31:15.940
“KILLING IS DISTASTEFUL!”

00:31:15.940 --> 00:31:19.269
OK, calm down dude, if you wake up your parents
the sleepover’s gonna be over.

00:31:19.269 --> 00:31:23.460
But the fact that John physically starts a
machine designed to drill through Jeff’s

00:31:23.460 --> 00:31:25.980
head is no different than him pulling a trigger
and shooting someone.

00:31:25.980 --> 00:31:28.429
“I’ve never murdered anyone in my life.

00:31:28.429 --> 00:31:30.457
The decisions are up to them.”

00:31:30.457 --> 00:31:34.055
From what we can tell, Jeff never had the
option to escape as many of the others did.

00:31:34.220 --> 00:31:36.090
Because if someone else were doing this, John

00:31:36.090 --> 00:31:37.090
would see it as unjust.

00:31:37.090 --> 00:31:40.769
But because Sing and Tapp are coming after
him, and he views himself as a God, he’ll

00:31:40.769 --> 00:31:42.740
break any rules he wants to bring them down.

00:31:42.740 --> 00:31:46.779
My favorite example of a God-complex in fiction
is Light Yagami from Death Note, and we see

00:31:46.779 --> 00:31:48.379
a similar thing happen with him.

00:31:48.379 --> 00:31:52.239
He starts off by only killing criminals, but
then he tries to kill the detective, L, who

00:31:52.239 --> 00:31:53.899
tries to bring him to justice.

00:31:53.899 --> 00:31:57.600
Jigsaw’s way of testing the two cops is
to see if they try to save Jeff or capture

00:31:57.600 --> 00:31:58.600
Jigsaw.

00:31:58.600 --> 00:32:01.830
Sing focuses on freeing the victim, but Tapp
goes after John, and as a result, fails the

00:32:01.830 --> 00:32:03.559
test and gets his throat slashed.

00:32:03.559 --> 00:32:07.159
Then Sing makes the same mistake and goes
after John, probably not wanting the mission

00:32:07.159 --> 00:32:08.220
to have been in vain.

00:32:08.220 --> 00:32:12.129
But John, who was always prepared for any
scenario, was prepared for this too.

00:32:12.129 --> 00:32:16.059
Sing chases him down the stairs into a hallway,
where the Quadruple Gun trap is set up.

00:32:16.059 --> 00:32:19.590
This one is pretty simple, if you trip a hidden
fishing wire, these guns hidden overhead will

00:32:19.590 --> 00:32:20.590
kill you.

00:32:20.590 --> 00:32:23.299
John steps over the wire safely, and Sing
shoots him with his own gun.

00:32:23.299 --> 00:32:26.940
John’s bulletproof vest absorbs the gunshot,
but he wisely stays on the ground and waits

00:32:26.940 --> 00:32:29.821
for Sing to approach, trip the wire, and get
himself killed…

00:32:29.821 --> 00:32:36.219
"Game. Over. Hahahahahahahahahaha!"

00:32:36.219 --> 00:32:39.320
...before getting back up and fleeing the
workshop for good.

00:32:39.320 --> 00:32:42.650
I think one of the reasons he believed he’d
be able to pull something like this off, was

00:32:42.650 --> 00:32:45.929
that he had endured so much pain from his
cancer treatment, that getting knocked to

00:32:45.929 --> 00:32:49.730
the ground with a gunshot impact, even at
the frail age of 50 at this point, was not

00:32:49.730 --> 00:32:51.000
much in comparison.

00:32:51.000 --> 00:32:53.840
He expresses a similar sentiment during another
game a year later.

00:32:53.840 --> 00:32:57.059
“I don't intend to mock you, officer…
but I'm a cancer patient.

00:32:57.059 --> 00:33:02.080
How could you possibly put me in any more
pain… than I'm already in?”

00:33:02.080 --> 00:33:05.389
Detective Tapp ends up surviving the throat
slash, so John has to abandon his workshop

00:33:05.389 --> 00:33:08.909
at the mannequin factory and relocate to a
property that would later be called The Nerve

00:33:08.909 --> 00:33:09.909
Gas House.

00:33:09.909 --> 00:33:13.090
I would theorize that this was part of the
Urban Renewal project, the housing project

00:33:13.090 --> 00:33:15.290
he abandoned at the end of his engineer career.

00:33:15.290 --> 00:33:18.649
There seem to be several of these houses throughout
the city, but this particular one has been

00:33:18.649 --> 00:33:22.620
outfitted with a network of underground tunnels
and hidden rooms, and one of these rooms was

00:33:22.620 --> 00:33:28.109
a dilapidated bathroom that John had perfectly
configured to the site of the next big game.

00:33:40.080 --> 00:33:44.520
If Jigsaw’s life is a puzzle, a combination
of the various pieces that make up his identity,

00:33:44.520 --> 00:33:47.799
we need to assemble those pieces in order
to fully understand him.

00:33:47.799 --> 00:33:50.879
The same approach can be taken to understand
some of his games.

00:33:50.879 --> 00:33:54.299
The Barn Game brought together people who
had wronged others but refused to admit their

00:33:54.299 --> 00:33:56.609
mistakes and seeked a confession from each
of them.

00:33:56.609 --> 00:34:00.619
They were all unified by that, but were otherwise
not connected in any significant way.

00:34:00.619 --> 00:34:05.619
So for John’s next game, the Bathroom Game
of October 2004, he strategically chose subjects

00:34:05.619 --> 00:34:09.220
who were all different pieces of the same
puzzle, and the centerpiece that connected

00:34:09.220 --> 00:34:14.060
to all the others was his oncologist at the
Angel of Mercy Hospital, Dr. Lawrence Gordon.

00:34:14.060 --> 00:34:17.040
The first subject that John captured for this
game was named Zep Hindle.

00:34:17.040 --> 00:34:20.840
He was an orderly at the hospital who actually
cared for John a lot and treated him well,

00:34:20.840 --> 00:34:24.290
but unfortunately for him, John kind of needed
him to make the whole thing work.

00:34:24.290 --> 00:34:28.160
We don’t find out why Zep was tested by
Jigsaw, however, this is another one where

00:34:28.160 --> 00:34:31.919
we can turn to the supplemental non-canon
material for possible clues.

00:34:31.919 --> 00:34:36.310
Saw: Rebirth was a comic and eventually motion
comic that aimed to give a little more backstory

00:34:36.310 --> 00:34:37.400
about John Kramer.

00:34:37.400 --> 00:34:40.910
This isn’t an official entry in the series,
because it does contradict details from some

00:34:40.910 --> 00:34:44.010
of the movies, but I think it’s relatively
harmless to use it’s explanation of why

00:34:44.010 --> 00:34:45.390
Jigsaw decided to test Zep.

00:34:45.390 --> 00:34:49.580
I’m gonna roll the clip, but as a fair warning,
the casting of the voices isn’t the best.

00:34:49.580 --> 00:34:53.260
The first voice you’re gonna hear is supposed
to be Zep and the narrator is John Kramer.

00:34:53.260 --> 00:34:55.698
So with that in mind, let’s roll the clip.

00:34:56.626 --> 00:35:00.644
“I bet the doc was a real shoulder to cry
on huh?

00:35:00.644 --> 00:35:02.540
Cold hearted bastards the lot off them.”

00:35:02.540 --> 00:35:03.980
“What are you talking about?”

00:35:03.980 --> 00:35:06.190
“They’re all screwing around on their
wives.

00:35:06.190 --> 00:35:09.840
I sure won’t be that way when I’m a doctor.”

00:35:09.840 --> 00:35:11.591
“The orderly had issues of his own.

00:35:11.591 --> 00:35:17.010
Now that my own life was slipping away, I
paid closer attention to the lives of others.”

00:35:17.010 --> 00:35:19.590
So it seems like Zep’s big flaw was that
he was a gossip.

00:35:19.590 --> 00:35:22.980
Jigsaw injects him with a poison and forces
him to help facilitate the game if he wants

00:35:22.980 --> 00:35:23.980
to get the antidote.

00:35:23.980 --> 00:35:28.450
Zep was most likely responsible for kidnapping
Dr. Gordon, while Amanda’s job was to get

00:35:28.450 --> 00:35:29.450
Adam Stanheight.

00:35:29.450 --> 00:35:33.340
Adam was a photographer hired by Detective
Tapp to spy on Gordon, because Tapp suspected

00:35:33.340 --> 00:35:34.870
Gordon of being Jigsaw.

00:35:34.870 --> 00:35:38.790
Before Amanda abducted him though, John performs
a ceremony to celebrate her rebirth.

00:35:38.790 --> 00:35:43.000
The ceremony seems to be another example of
John trying to make his MO into a religious

00:35:43.000 --> 00:35:44.000
experience.

00:35:44.000 --> 00:35:47.080
He dons the black and red robes yet again
in a candle lit room and asks her to essentially

00:35:47.080 --> 00:35:48.970
make vows of devotion to him.

00:35:48.970 --> 00:35:52.510
Interestingly, in the Saw III official soundtrack,
the music that plays during this scene is

00:35:52.510 --> 00:35:56.090
called “Baptism,” and if you listen closely,
there’s a choral chant in the background,

00:35:56.090 --> 00:35:57.708
giving the feeling of a church choir.

00:35:57.708 --> 00:36:07.620
🎵 "Baptism" - Charlie Clouser 🎵

00:36:07.620 --> 00:36:10.720
He leaves Amanda to it, and heads to The Bathroom
to make the final preparations.

00:36:10.720 --> 00:36:14.070
When she shows up with the unconscious Adam,
he pauses the Glam &amp; Gore tutorial he was

00:36:14.070 --> 00:36:15.070
watching…

00:36:15.070 --> 00:36:17.310
He instructs her on what
to do with Adam as he pours a bucket of fake

00:36:17.310 --> 00:36:20.730
blood on the ground and prepares himself for
his most ambitious game yet.

00:36:20.730 --> 00:36:22.480
“It’s time to start our game.”

00:36:22.480 --> 00:36:24.610
Oh boy, I’ll get the controllers!

00:36:24.610 --> 00:36:26.563
TAPP: "I won't play your game. I won't!

00:36:26.884 --> 00:36:28.141
Aughhh!"

00:36:28.141 --> 00:36:29.721
CZ (v/o): Ohhhh wait.

00:36:29.721 --> 00:36:31.160
I think I misunderstood.

00:36:31.160 --> 00:36:34.280
John injects himself with a serum that is
supposed to slow down his heart rate, relax

00:36:34.280 --> 00:36:38.660
his muscles and make him less noticeable as
a he pretends, key word: pretends, to be dead

00:36:38.660 --> 00:36:41.900
on the floor in the middle of the bathroom
and Amanda takes all the other materials,

00:36:41.900 --> 00:36:45.990
hits the light and closes the door on Lawrence,
Adam and John, who has a gun in his left hand

00:36:45.990 --> 00:36:47.300
and a tape recorder in the other.

00:36:47.300 --> 00:36:50.710
It would seem that he’s also hiding a small
remote in his palm or something, that has

00:36:50.710 --> 00:36:54.640
the ability to send a shock to Adam or Lawrence
all Jose Altuve style.

00:36:54.640 --> 00:36:57.890
The goal for Lawrence in this game was to
kill Adam before time runs out, and the goal

00:36:57.890 --> 00:36:59.290
for Adam was just to escape.

00:36:59.290 --> 00:37:04.240
He was tested because he spent more time spying
on other people than examining his own life.

00:37:04.240 --> 00:37:07.160
Adam and Gordon are supposed to be enemies
in this game, but they try to secretly work

00:37:07.160 --> 00:37:11.280
together to escape, not knowing that the man
in the center of the room is alive, listening,

00:37:11.280 --> 00:37:13.560
and also the man responsible for their imprisonment.

00:37:13.560 --> 00:37:16.910
So when they develop a plan to make it look
like Lawrence had killed Adam with the poison

00:37:16.910 --> 00:37:20.730
to try to fool Zep, who was watching via the
camera, it doesn’t work, because John hears

00:37:20.730 --> 00:37:24.440
everything they said, and shocks Adam to show
Zep that he wasn’t really dead.

00:37:24.440 --> 00:37:27.126
Later, when Lawrence seems to have lost all
hope, Jigsaw gives him a buzz

00:37:29.704 --> 00:37:34.160
which I saw as him trying one last ditch effort
to reinvigorate Gordon’s passion, to make

00:37:34.160 --> 00:37:38.577
him stop feeling sorry for himself and to ignite
a fury to motivate him to try to pass his test.

00:37:38.577 --> 00:37:40.000
I’d say it works.

00:37:40.000 --> 00:37:45.980
OK, fine, roll the clip one last time.

00:37:46.275 --> 00:37:50.626
*screaming like a madman*

00:37:53.090 --> 00:37:54.090
That never gets old.

00:37:54.090 --> 00:37:57.930
Gordon ends up cutting off his own foot to
escape the shackle, and in one desperate final

00:37:57.930 --> 00:38:02.030
attempt to save his family, pretends to kill
Adam again, this time using the gun.

00:38:02.030 --> 00:38:06.190
I find it very interesting that John doesn’t
use the electric shock again to test if Adam

00:38:06.190 --> 00:38:07.190
is really dead.

00:38:07.190 --> 00:38:09.220
It might be that he actually doesn’t suspect
it.

00:38:09.220 --> 00:38:12.430
The first time, he knew to be skeptical because
he could hear Lawrence and Adam whispering

00:38:12.430 --> 00:38:13.430
to each other in the dark.

00:38:13.430 --> 00:38:17.210
But on the second attempt, I’m pretty sure that
Dr. Gordon just gives Adam a wink; I’ve

00:38:17.210 --> 00:38:20.220
theorized that it’s while his head is turned
away from the camera right here.

00:38:20.220 --> 00:38:23.780
John has to keep his eyes closed, so he doesn’t
know that this was another fake out attempt,

00:38:23.780 --> 00:38:26.170
and Lawrence’s acting was good enough to
sell that it was real.

00:38:26.170 --> 00:38:29.340
I know there are going to be people who think
it’s out of character for someone as smart

00:38:29.340 --> 00:38:32.800
as John to be fooled like that, so if you
have your own theory as to why he didn’t

00:38:32.800 --> 00:38:34.780
shock Adam right here, let me know if the
comments.

00:38:34.780 --> 00:38:38.490
At the end of the game, Dr. Gordon is the
only one who manages to limp away alive, and

00:38:38.490 --> 00:38:42.250
that leaves Adam alone in the bathroom with
John, who Adam still believes to be dead.

00:38:42.250 --> 00:38:45.018
Then, this happens.

00:38:53.496 --> 00:38:58.290
I swear, this isn’t the beginning of a mattress
commercial, THIS IS WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENS…...

00:38:58.290 --> 00:39:02.225
And if you do get a mattress commercial, I
swear it’s a complete coincidence.

00:39:17.310 --> 00:39:21.150
After getting to his feet, Jigsaw informs
Adam that the key to his chain was inside

00:39:21.150 --> 00:39:24.720
the bathtub, which was now unreachable because
the tub had drained.

00:39:24.720 --> 00:39:28.580
Adam tries to grab Zep’s gun off the ground
to attack Jigsaw, but one last electric shock

00:39:28.580 --> 00:39:30.159
sends it flying from his hands.

00:39:30.159 --> 00:39:31.722
JIGSAW: “Game over.”

00:39:31.750 --> 00:39:33.750
ADAM: (YouTube Poop scream)

00:39:34.630 --> 00:39:38.350
John was now out of danger, but he was not
done with his tasks for that evening.

00:39:38.350 --> 00:39:40.670
He leaves the bathroom to go find Dr. Gordon.

00:39:40.670 --> 00:39:44.410
After seeing the way the Dr. had handled the
situation under pressure, he realized he would

00:39:44.410 --> 00:39:48.370
be an excellent ally, and having passed his
test, he’d be a prime candidate to become

00:39:48.370 --> 00:39:49.520
a new disciple.

00:39:49.520 --> 00:39:53.000
He catches up to him, and finds him on the
verge of passing out because of the blood loss.

00:39:53.000 --> 00:39:56.480
John splashes some water on his face while
congratulating him on surviving.

00:39:56.480 --> 00:40:00.020
He helps clean up the wound and eventually
physically rehabilitates him, giving him a

00:40:00.020 --> 00:40:02.810
prosthetic foot and taking him on as his next
accomplice.

00:40:02.810 --> 00:40:05.560
John would treat Dr. Gordon differently than
his other students.

00:40:05.560 --> 00:40:09.620
He was already beginning to sense potential
problems with Mark and Amanda, who he suspected

00:40:09.620 --> 00:40:13.650
of having dark ulterior motives to harm the
victims of the traps rather than save them.

00:40:13.650 --> 00:40:18.930
He feared that his platform, the name Jigsaw,
could be misused after his passing, so using

00:40:18.930 --> 00:40:21.370
Dr. Gordon, he set up a system of checks and
balances.

00:40:21.370 --> 00:40:24.870
By keeping Gordon’s involvement a secret
from the other apprentices, he had a hidden

00:40:24.870 --> 00:40:26.610
weapon to help preserve his legacy.

00:40:26.610 --> 00:40:30.790
I should note that Nelson was still overseas
fighting in America’s Iraq war, so John

00:40:30.790 --> 00:40:33.910
didn’t know if he’d be coming back or
if he would be reliable anymore.

00:40:33.910 --> 00:40:37.960
At some point over the next year, Jigsaw continues
carrying out smaller traps to test the people

00:40:37.960 --> 00:40:40.570
he deems to have lost their appreciation for
life.

00:40:40.570 --> 00:40:44.360
One of these is a woman named Joan, who survived
her trap, but decided not to become one of

00:40:44.360 --> 00:40:46.310
Jigsaw’s followers for unknown reasons.

00:40:46.310 --> 00:40:51.115
She does, however, gain a stronger appreciation
for her life, and tells her story on the news.

00:40:53.095 --> 00:40:57.900
"That pure horror of absolute horror gave me light,

00:40:57.900 --> 00:41:03.160
and as wrong as this may seem, I'm better for enduring it."

00:41:03.160 --> 00:41:07.500
The broadcast reaches a man named Bobby Dagen,
who is inspired by her transformation and,

00:41:07.500 --> 00:41:10.520
perhaps more significantly, her potential
marketability.

00:41:10.520 --> 00:41:14.370
The smart thing for Bobby to do would be to
get in contact with her and offer to ghost-write

00:41:14.370 --> 00:41:18.480
a book about her Jigsaw experience for a percentage
of the profits, but what he does instead is

00:41:18.480 --> 00:41:21.860
write his own book, where he pretends to be
a Jigsaw victim.

00:41:21.860 --> 00:41:25.470
John takes issue with this for similar reasons
to him taking issue with Hoffman impersonating

00:41:25.470 --> 00:41:28.180
one of his traps, and confronts him at a book
signing.

00:41:28.180 --> 00:41:32.491
“In Ancient Egypt, if you were speaking
under oath, you were required to say, ‘if

00:41:32.491 --> 00:41:36.853
I’m lying, take me to the quarries.’

00:41:37.627 --> 00:41:39.050
That mean anything to you?”

00:41:39.050 --> 00:41:42.400
After getting his copy signed, John removes
the cover, with the photo of Bobby’s face

00:41:42.400 --> 00:41:45.060
on it, telling him that he wouldn’t need
it now that they’ve met.

00:41:45.060 --> 00:41:48.760
I think that this is John’s little way of
telling Bobby that he’s the real Jigsaw.

00:41:48.760 --> 00:41:52.060
Obviously Bobby isn’t supposed to figure
it out right away, but he’s basically saying

00:41:52.060 --> 00:41:55.710
that he’s so intelligent, that he’ll always
remember Bobby’s face, even from such a

00:41:55.710 --> 00:41:58.890
short meeting, and he’s kind of hinting
that they could meet again.

00:41:58.890 --> 00:42:03.130
They don’t meet again though, the task of
testing Bobby Dagen would fall on one of Jigsaw’s

00:42:03.130 --> 00:42:04.130
disciples.

00:42:04.130 --> 00:42:07.150
The next big game John would plan would be
even more complex than the last.

00:42:07.150 --> 00:42:10.510
This game would involve two locations, and
as with the bathroom game, he planned to place

00:42:10.510 --> 00:42:13.200
himself in the center of one of them to facilitate
things.

00:42:13.200 --> 00:42:16.330
He also placed Amanda in the midst of the
action in the other location to make sure

00:42:16.330 --> 00:42:17.770
that rules were followed.

00:42:17.770 --> 00:42:21.510
Around October of 2005, it was finally time
for the game to take place.

00:42:21.510 --> 00:42:25.290
The first half of the game, which was created
by Jigsaw, takes place in the previously mentioned

00:42:25.290 --> 00:42:29.430
Nerve Gas House, and contained a series of
criminals who all had ties to one cop named

00:42:29.430 --> 00:42:30.540
Eric Matthews.

00:42:30.540 --> 00:42:33.970
One of these criminals was a con man named
Obi Tate, who John convinced to help kidnap

00:42:33.970 --> 00:42:35.240
the other seven players.

00:42:35.240 --> 00:42:39.950
Then, John brought in Hoffman to sedate and
bring in Obi as the eighth and final contestant.

00:42:39.950 --> 00:42:43.480
After some finishing touches to one of the
traps within the game called the Magnum Eyehole,

00:42:43.480 --> 00:42:45.060
the Nerve Gas House was ready.

00:42:45.060 --> 00:42:48.780
In this game, each member was breathing in
a deadly nerve gas, and was tasked with completing

00:42:48.780 --> 00:42:51.290
a trap of their own to win an antidote.

00:42:51.290 --> 00:42:54.880
Each of them was a real criminal who was framed
for a different crime they did not commit

00:42:54.880 --> 00:42:57.320
by Eric Matthews, except for one.

00:42:57.320 --> 00:42:59.310
Daniel Matthews was Eric Mathews son.

00:42:59.310 --> 00:43:02.170
He was also a criminal, although his crimes
were much more childish.

00:43:02.170 --> 00:43:05.720
Part of the game involved them all figuring
out that they were tied to Matthews in some

00:43:05.720 --> 00:43:06.720
way.

00:43:06.720 --> 00:43:08.040
The second half of the game was created by
Amanda.

00:43:08.040 --> 00:43:11.830
So Amanda was inside of John’s portion of
the game, and John was inside Amanda’s portion.

00:43:11.830 --> 00:43:15.370
The second half took place at an unused Steel
Plant called Wilson Steel, which had been

00:43:15.370 --> 00:43:18.510
the location of John’s main workshop over
the last year.

00:43:18.510 --> 00:43:21.900
Amanda, possibly with the help of John, had
set up video monitors of the events that had

00:43:21.900 --> 00:43:23.960
already taken place at the Nerve Gas House.

00:43:23.960 --> 00:43:27.330
This was the main motivation for Detective
Matthews to participate in the game.

00:43:27.330 --> 00:43:30.020
He would see his son in danger and be forced
to play along.

00:43:30.020 --> 00:43:33.858
To add insult to injury, he re-recorded Daniel’s
voicemail greeting…?

00:43:33.858 --> 00:43:35.240
JIGSAW: “You’ve reached Daniel’s phone, he’s
not in right now.

00:43:35.240 --> 00:43:37.570
But if you--”

00:43:37.570 --> 00:43:40.340
That actually brings up a lot of questions
for me.

00:43:40.340 --> 00:43:43.060
Like, did he re-record the voicemails of every
victim?

00:43:43.060 --> 00:43:47.606
And if so, why wasn’t that included as bonus
content on the special edition DVDs of each

00:43:47.606 --> 00:43:48.328
Saw movie?

00:43:48.328 --> 00:43:51.679
“Promotional DVD.”

00:43:51.679 --> 00:43:58.513
JIGSAW: "Hello. You've reached the phone of Zac Morris. He's not in right now cause he didn't agree with my opinion on Saw 7.

00:43:58.513 --> 00:44:01.950
Amanda is able to get Daniel through John’s
half of the game at the Nerve Gas House, and

00:44:01.950 --> 00:44:04.840
Daniel is stowed safely and secretly within
Jigsaw’s headquarters.

00:44:04.840 --> 00:44:09.740
But to lure Detective Matthews into his trap,
John uses another trap, which contains a clue

00:44:09.740 --> 00:44:12.274
about the location of Jigsaw’s workshop.

00:44:19.390 --> 00:44:23.420
Jigsaw would, for the first time in his known
history, enlist the help of his secret asset,

00:44:23.420 --> 00:44:25.850
Dr. Lawrence Gordon for one of his traps.

00:44:25.850 --> 00:44:29.340
The victim this time was named Michael Marks,
a police informant who was another former

00:44:29.340 --> 00:44:31.380
patient of Homeward Bound clinic.

00:44:31.380 --> 00:44:35.070
Jigsaw felt Michael was not worthy of the
life he’d been given because as an informant,

00:44:35.070 --> 00:44:38.950
he spent all his time spying on others and
had become a rat or a snitch.

00:44:38.950 --> 00:44:42.490
This shows us that Jigsaw has gone even further
down the rabbit hole.

00:44:42.490 --> 00:44:46.060
John does exactly what Michael Marks does
to find victims who he believes are wrong

00:44:46.060 --> 00:44:47.060
do-ers.

00:44:47.060 --> 00:44:50.640
If anything, John himself is more guilty of
this because of the number of people he’s

00:44:50.640 --> 00:44:51.640
keeping tabs on.

00:44:51.640 --> 00:44:55.580
But his reasoning goes back, once again, to
the God-complex, causing him to believe that

00:44:55.580 --> 00:44:59.000
he’s allowed to do it, but others, or society
as a whole, is not.

00:44:59.000 --> 00:45:02.490
Michael wakes up wearing a device around his
neck called the Venus Fly Trap, which will

00:45:02.490 --> 00:45:06.560
clamp down and impale his face if he’s unable
to obtain the key, which Gordon has hidden

00:45:06.560 --> 00:45:07.810
behind his right eye.

00:45:07.810 --> 00:45:11.800
Jigsaw asks him to look inward, rather than
outward, and give up one of the eyes that

00:45:11.800 --> 00:45:14.280
he relies on so much to spy on criminals.

00:45:14.280 --> 00:45:18.170
Michael fails his test, and John takes a Jigsaw
piece out of him and leaves a message behind

00:45:18.170 --> 00:45:20.570
for Detective Matthews, telling him to look
closer.

00:45:20.570 --> 00:45:24.650
I also wonder if his mis-spelling of Matthews's
last name was another sign that the brain

00:45:24.650 --> 00:45:26.450
cancer was really getting to his head.

00:45:26.450 --> 00:45:30.310
Matthews would take a closer look, and discover
that the victim was one of his informants,

00:45:30.310 --> 00:45:34.040
and that the steel used to construct the trap
was from Wilson Steel Plant, a location that

00:45:34.040 --> 00:45:38.340
John knew Matthews was familiar with because
it played a part in a case from his past.

00:45:38.340 --> 00:45:41.420
Matthews leads his team there just in time
to catch Jigsaw eating his Sunday morning

00:45:41.420 --> 00:45:42.758
Cocoa Puffs.

00:45:42.758 --> 00:45:46.663
"I am cuckoo for Cocoa Puffs. I'M CUCKOO FOR COCOA PUFFS! CUCKOO FOR COCOA PUFFFS!!"

00:45:46.663 --> 00:45:52.350
*maniacal laughing* I’m sorry, I’m just imagining
John Kramer doing that.

00:45:52.350 --> 00:45:54.520
*more laughter* 

00:45:54.520 --> 00:45:59.040
Just seeing this old cancer patient just start
jumping around and losing it when he tastes

00:45:59.040 --> 00:46:01.090
the Cocoa--

00:46:01.090 --> 00:46:03.760
The SWAT team comes in and handcuffs Jigsaw.

00:46:03.760 --> 00:46:06.010
Matthews mocks him by learning in and saying,

00:46:06.010 --> 00:46:07.250
“Is this close enough?”

00:46:07.250 --> 00:46:09.468
ADAM: “Uhm… yeah.”

00:46:09.468 --> 00:46:13.700
Matthews orders his men to book Jigsaw, but
as I mentioned earlier in this lesson, John

00:46:13.700 --> 00:46:17.350
takes control of the situation by saying he’ll
have to stay in place.

00:46:17.350 --> 00:46:20.850
The cops find the video monitors and John
confirms that the kid seen on the screens

00:46:20.850 --> 00:46:22.890
is indeed Matthews’s son Daniel.

00:46:22.890 --> 00:46:26.860
His facial expression as he does this is a
sick example of how his psychotic tendencies

00:46:26.860 --> 00:46:27.860
have evolved.

00:46:27.860 --> 00:46:32.350
I spoke earlier about the increasing need
for repeated stimulation sometimes seen in

00:46:32.350 --> 00:46:33.350
psychopaths.

00:46:33.350 --> 00:46:36.080
This occurs because at the beginning, John
believed he was doing the world a service

00:46:36.080 --> 00:46:39.600
by punishing criminals and other people he’s
judged to have lost their way.

00:46:39.600 --> 00:46:44.250
He tortured these individuals using his traps,
and so his brain came to associate doing a

00:46:44.250 --> 00:46:47.680
good thing with doing a very bad thing: putting
others in pain.

00:46:47.680 --> 00:46:50.990
So as a result, he starts to like the idea
of hurting his victims.

00:46:50.990 --> 00:46:53.810
“It’s your son Daniel, you remember him
don’t you?”

00:46:53.810 --> 00:46:56.610
“I know who he is you piece of ****. What
is he doing on that ****ing monitor?”

00:46:56.610 --> 00:47:00.090
“Well, I haven’t looked at the monitors
for some time, so it would be hard for me

00:47:00.090 --> 00:47:05.440
to say, but I would imagine that he’s cowering
in a corner with a look on his face…”

00:47:05.440 --> 00:47:07.140
“You mother****er where is he?”

00:47:07.140 --> 00:47:10.880
And he has an even bigger smile on his face
when he describes the torture that Daniel

00:47:10.880 --> 00:47:12.600
might be going through in detail.

00:47:12.600 --> 00:47:18.670
He has about two hours before the gas creeping
into his nervous system begins to break down

00:47:18.670 --> 00:47:22.540
his body tissue, and he begins to bleed from
every orpheus he has.

00:47:23.680 --> 00:47:24.820
Oh yes.

00:47:25.439 --> 00:47:27.569
There will be blood.”

00:47:27.569 --> 00:47:31.000
I feel like there’s a Paul Thomas Anderson
joke to be made here, but I don’t know what

00:47:31.000 --> 00:47:35.000
it is, so I’m just gonna put this humorous
if not irrelevant meme.

00:47:35.000 --> 00:47:38.280
Alright, I think that’s been on screen for
long enough.

00:47:38.280 --> 00:47:41.570
John explains to Matthews how he can see his
son again, if he simply sits and talks with

00:47:41.570 --> 00:47:44.790
John until the game ends without resorting
to dirty police work such as…

00:47:44.790 --> 00:47:46.316
“Evidence tampering.”

00:47:46.316 --> 00:47:47.571
Ha, I bet you thought I was going to say,

00:47:47.571 --> 00:47:48.870
"BRUTALITY!"

00:47:48.870 --> 00:47:52.010
Matthews reluctantly agrees to sit down with
Jigsaw, who tries to get through to him and

00:47:52.010 --> 00:47:54.220
make him realize the error of his past ways.

00:47:54.220 --> 00:47:58.290
For how far John has strayed from his original
intention to help people, I do think he actually

00:47:58.290 --> 00:48:01.350
does a good job during this game of staying
focused and doing his best to get Matthews

00:48:01.350 --> 00:48:02.790
to actually win the game.

00:48:02.790 --> 00:48:06.470
We also learn a little bit more about Jigsaw’s
mantra, the reason that he wants to build a

00:48:06.470 --> 00:48:09.070
following and try to change da world.

00:48:09.070 --> 00:48:13.480
He explains that Charles Darwin’s theory
of evolution no longer applies to the modern

00:48:13.480 --> 00:48:17.240
man, because we live in a society where it’s
easy to survive without having the edge, or

00:48:17.240 --> 00:48:18.240
will to survive.

00:48:18.240 --> 00:48:21.090
That’s why John views his subjects as having
not cherished their lives.

00:48:21.090 --> 00:48:25.300
Then he goes onto explain that his past, with
the cancer and the lost child changed that

00:48:25.300 --> 00:48:29.070
for him, but before he’s able to give Matthews
that same epiphany, the detective walks away

00:48:29.070 --> 00:48:30.070
in a rage.

00:48:30.070 --> 00:48:33.890
That would be the closest John would get to
converting him to the church of Jigsaw.

00:48:33.890 --> 00:48:37.310
Eric ends up resorting to destroying John’s
blueprints, which John points out is not the

00:48:37.310 --> 00:48:40.270
proper move from an officer who should be
collecting evidence.

00:48:40.270 --> 00:48:44.350
But John really wants Eric to succeed, so
he gives him another chance to turn it around.

00:48:44.350 --> 00:48:48.051
Eventually, Matthews snaps when he sees a
criminal on the monitor coming after his son

00:48:48.051 --> 00:48:51.150
and decides to go with his go-to method: “BRUTALITY!”

00:48:51.150 --> 00:48:55.430
He breaks John’s finger, destroys the walkie-talkie,
which is basically his way of saying he won’t

00:48:55.430 --> 00:48:59.160
be doing things by the book anymore, and puts
his gun into John’s mouth as he continually

00:48:59.160 --> 00:49:00.160
threatens him.

00:49:00.160 --> 00:49:02.070
At that point, John has seen enough.

00:49:02.070 --> 00:49:05.966
He’s realized that Matthews is past the
point of no return, and that there is no hope

00:49:05.966 --> 00:49:07.106
for him.

00:49:07.106 --> 00:49:10.000
“Game… game over.”

00:49:18.450 --> 00:49:22.210
Jigsaw realized that there was no hope for
Detective Eric Matthews after he turned a

00:49:22.210 --> 00:49:25.770
violent hand against him, and decided it was
time to take him to the house where the Nerve

00:49:25.770 --> 00:49:27.370
Gas Game had been held.

00:49:27.370 --> 00:49:31.150
This was all part of his game plan though…
or I guess technically Amanda’s game plan,

00:49:31.150 --> 00:49:34.090
though it’s hard to imagine that John didn’t
play a big part in it.

00:49:34.090 --> 00:49:38.500
Because John’s most dangerous asset is,
unlike many other horror movie villains, his

00:49:38.500 --> 00:49:39.500
intelligence.

00:49:39.500 --> 00:49:43.240
We’ve seen him use his masterful understanding
of engineering to his advantage, but he was

00:49:43.240 --> 00:49:46.300
also helped by an impressive comprehension
of the human mind.

00:49:46.300 --> 00:49:50.250
To put it into a term that I find to be almost
comically appropriate, I would say that John

00:49:50.250 --> 00:49:52.280
was a master of Game Theory.

00:49:52.280 --> 00:49:55.380
“Hello internet, welcome to Game Theory.

00:49:55.380 --> 00:50:00.500
So I’ve been doing some research and I found
out that what if Shaggy from Scooby Doo was

00:50:00.500 --> 00:50:02.390
a stoner the whole time?”

00:50:02.390 --> 00:50:04.780
Haha, no, that’s offensive.

00:50:04.780 --> 00:50:10.870
I am not a stoner don’t do drugs or you
might wake up with a reverse bear trap.

00:50:10.870 --> 00:50:15.360
But I recently learned that the beloved internet
show Game Theory is actually named after an

00:50:15.360 --> 00:50:18.360
actual concept called Game Theory.

00:50:18.360 --> 00:50:21.130
And yes, I do plan on continuing to pronounce
it like that.

00:50:21.130 --> 00:50:25.350
GAME THEORY is the study of how players in
a game will strategize in different situations.

00:50:25.350 --> 00:50:28.010
It’s basically the science of decision making.

00:50:28.010 --> 00:50:33.790
The development of Game Theory was first developed
by mathematician John Von Neumann to try to

00:50:33.790 --> 00:50:35.400
bolster his Poker skills.

00:50:35.400 --> 00:50:38.840
John Kramer used some of those concepts to
make his games adaptable to some of the most

00:50:38.840 --> 00:50:41.110
likely decisions that players may make.

00:50:41.110 --> 00:50:45.950
He’s thought out most if not all possible
outcomes for each decision, but uses GAME

00:50:45.950 --> 00:50:50.720
THEORY to determine which scenarios are most
likely to happen and spend the most time developing

00:50:50.720 --> 00:50:51.870
those outcomes.

00:50:51.870 --> 00:50:55.660
Yes, it is more complicated than that, but
as I’ve said before, we don’t do math

00:50:55.660 --> 00:50:59.130
here in the Horror History classroom, so I’ll
leave it in the simplest terms.

00:50:59.130 --> 00:51:04.010
John’s understanding of Game Theory is the
reason he was able to side-step Cecil, the

00:51:04.010 --> 00:51:07.570
reason he could count on Zep to show up in
the bathroom and the reason that he was comfortable

00:51:07.570 --> 00:51:10.020
putting his life on the line at The Wilson
Steel Plant.

00:51:10.020 --> 00:51:14.130
When Matthews loses his game, John has already
predicted that Matthews will do what benefits

00:51:14.130 --> 00:51:17.600
him most in the moment, by threatening John
and forcing him to give directions to the

00:51:17.600 --> 00:51:18.880
Nerve Gas House.

00:51:18.880 --> 00:51:22.310
John uses the fact that Matthews was thinking
independently from the rest of his unit to

00:51:22.310 --> 00:51:26.000
his advantage; while John takes him to the
real Nerve Gas House, the police tech team

00:51:26.000 --> 00:51:29.730
follows the video signal to another house,
where the pre-recorded videos are being played

00:51:29.730 --> 00:51:30.730
back from.

00:51:30.730 --> 00:51:34.170
Remember how I theorized that there were several
houses, all part of John’s Urban Renewal

00:51:34.170 --> 00:51:35.170
Project?

00:51:35.170 --> 00:51:38.110
I think the Fakeout Nerve Gas House is just another
one of these houses.

00:51:38.110 --> 00:51:41.940
When John and Matthews arrive at the real
house, John is hanging onto his life by a

00:51:41.940 --> 00:51:46.360
thread, and hands over a key, not disclosing
that this would be the key that locks in Eric

00:51:46.360 --> 00:51:48.190
Matthews’s fate.

00:51:49.304 --> 00:51:53.705
“Now you are locked away, helpless and alone.

00:51:53.705 --> 00:51:55.348
Game over!”

00:51:55.348 --> 00:51:58.051
🎵 "Forget To Remember" - Mudvayne 🎵

00:51:58.051 --> 00:51:59.930
That’s my favorite one, if you can’t tell.

00:51:59.930 --> 00:52:04.220
Amanda attempted to leave Eric Matthews for
dead, but Jigsaw, seemingly seeing great potential

00:52:04.220 --> 00:52:07.760
in the guy and perhaps sensing that he was
close to getting through to him, decided to

00:52:07.760 --> 00:52:09.400
give him one more chance.

00:52:09.400 --> 00:52:12.630
He saved Matthews and kept him in a holding
cell for the next six months.

00:52:12.630 --> 00:52:15.640
During this period, John realizes that he’s
running on borrowed time.

00:52:15.640 --> 00:52:19.200
He knows his days are extremely numbered at
this point and he still has many targets that

00:52:19.200 --> 00:52:20.320
he wants to punish.

00:52:20.320 --> 00:52:23.730
Most importantly though, he still needs to
decide which of his disciples, now consisting

00:52:23.730 --> 00:52:27.760
of Amanda Young, Mark Hoffman and Lawrence
Gordon, would continue his work after his

00:52:27.760 --> 00:52:28.760
death.

00:52:28.760 --> 00:52:30.430
He created games for each of them as a final
test.

00:52:30.430 --> 00:52:33.420
Amanda’s game was planned to take place
with John on his deathbed, while Hoffman’s

00:52:33.420 --> 00:52:35.080
would be a post-mortem challenge.

00:52:35.080 --> 00:52:38.080
It’s not clear if Gordon’s final test
was detailed in the films.

00:52:38.080 --> 00:52:41.460
It could be that the preparations he helped
with for some of the other traps were part

00:52:41.460 --> 00:52:44.370
of his final test, or it could be that it
happened off-screen.

00:52:44.370 --> 00:52:48.610
He also hoped to get his ex-wife back on his
side by showing her that his rehabilitation

00:52:48.610 --> 00:52:52.359
methods had saved Amanda, even when the medical
approach at Jill’s clinic could not.

00:52:52.359 --> 00:52:55.565
“I brought proof that it works.”

00:52:56.926 --> 00:52:59.102
JILL: “Amanda?”

00:52:59.102 --> 00:53:00.628
“Hello Jill.”

00:53:00.628 --> 00:53:04.890
But there are way more planned traps and games
that Jigsaw didn’t have time for in his

00:53:04.890 --> 00:53:05.890
lifetime.

00:53:05.890 --> 00:53:09.590
He records a tape for his ex-wife Jill and
leaves it for her in his will, instructing

00:53:09.590 --> 00:53:13.380
her to carry out a game to help balance the
power of Jigsaw when he’s gone.

00:53:13.380 --> 00:53:16.860
This included Hoffman’s final test, but
also five others who were a part of William

00:53:16.860 --> 00:53:20.010
Easton’s Umbrella Health, the insurance
company that had prohibited John from seeking

00:53:20.010 --> 00:53:21.940
out alternative treatments to his cancer.

00:53:21.940 --> 00:53:25.480
The box he leaves behind is locked so that
nobody without the key could get into it,

00:53:25.480 --> 00:53:27.790
and he would hold onto the key for a while
longer.

00:53:27.790 --> 00:53:31.500
He also makes pre-records the tapes that would
play during games and traps for other people

00:53:31.500 --> 00:53:35.850
like Detective Kerry, a repeat offender named
Troy, SWAT Officer Rigg, a guy named Trevor

00:53:35.850 --> 00:53:39.420
who we know nothing about, John’s former
business partner Art Blank, another pair of

00:53:39.420 --> 00:53:43.180
tapes for Trevor and Art Blank in case they
survive the first one, a pimp named Brenda,

00:53:43.180 --> 00:53:47.430
and evil Motel manager named Ivan, a pair
of abusive parents named Rex and Morgan, an

00:53:47.430 --> 00:53:51.500
FBI Agent named Lindsay Perez, another FBI
Agent named Peter Strahm, five citizens who

00:53:51.500 --> 00:53:55.210
all played a part in building fire scandal,
a malicious money lender named Simone, a malicious

00:53:55.210 --> 00:53:59.370
money lender named Eddie, a sensationalist
reporter named Pamela Jenkins, a love triangle

00:53:59.370 --> 00:54:03.450
consisting of three young people: Brad, Dina
and Ryan, a gang of four rap-metal lovin’

00:54:03.450 --> 00:54:07.580
racists and the man who once tried to pretend
to be a Jigsaw victim would finally become

00:54:07.580 --> 00:54:09.000
one: Bobby Dagen.

00:54:09.000 --> 00:54:13.630
Keep in mind Jigsaw didn’t assume the outcome
of any game, so he also probably had multiple

00:54:13.630 --> 00:54:17.460
tapes for each person to take all of the possible
results into account.

00:54:17.460 --> 00:54:21.930
In addition to ALL OF THAT, he left one final
set of instructions that Jill was supposed

00:54:21.930 --> 00:54:23.270
to hand off to Dr. Gordon.

00:54:23.270 --> 00:54:24.270
“Watch over Jill.

00:54:24.270 --> 00:54:29.760
And should anything happens to her, I want you to act immediately
on my behalf.

00:54:29.760 --> 00:54:35.280
In return for that, I will keep no more secrets
from you.”

00:54:35.280 --> 00:54:40.640
I hope old Johnny charged up some extra camera and audio recorder
batteries, because that’s a LOT of recording

00:54:40.640 --> 00:54:42.330
going on for Jigsaw....

00:54:42.330 --> 00:54:45.650
But not as much recording as I’ve had to
do to make this video, so with that in mind,

00:54:45.650 --> 00:54:50.050
I think it’s only fair that I take a little
break before we get to the final game of John’s life.

00:54:58.350 --> 00:55:04.140
It is likely that John knew the games taking
place in April of 2006 would be his last,

00:55:04.140 --> 00:55:05.260
regardless of the outcome.

00:55:05.260 --> 00:55:06.900
Two games would take place that day.

00:55:06.900 --> 00:55:11.070
The one involving Rigg, Blank, Matthews and
Hoffman was designed by John, but would be

00:55:11.070 --> 00:55:14.910
carried out mostly by Hoffman; while the other
game, involving Lynn Denlon, Jeff Denlon,

00:55:14.910 --> 00:55:19.220
Amanda Young and John, was created by John
and would be facilitated by John.

00:55:19.220 --> 00:55:22.220
The game was originally going to feature Jeff
Denlon going through a series of trials to

00:55:22.220 --> 00:55:25.880
try to forgive the people involved in a road
accident that resulted in his young son’s

00:55:25.880 --> 00:55:26.880
death.

00:55:26.880 --> 00:55:29.420
The idea was that if he made it to the end
of the game, he’d be forced to confront

00:55:29.420 --> 00:55:31.690
Amanda who is implied to be his captor.

00:55:31.690 --> 00:55:34.990
Jeff’s restraint would be tested by choosing
whether or not to kill Amanda upon reaching

00:55:34.990 --> 00:55:38.680
the end, while Amanda’s restraint would
be tested by making sure she didn’t sabotage

00:55:38.680 --> 00:55:41.680
Jeff’s trial as she did to some of her other
victims in the past.

00:55:41.680 --> 00:55:45.820
Jigsaw was worried that Amanda was only involved
because she enjoyed punishing the victims,

00:55:45.820 --> 00:55:50.190
and did not want to see them actually succeed,
pass their tests, and rehabilitate as she

00:55:50.190 --> 00:55:51.620
supposedly had.

00:55:51.620 --> 00:55:55.541
Seeing Amanda sabotage her recent traps to
make them unwinnable disturbed John, and may

00:55:55.541 --> 00:56:00.040
have made him start to lose faith in his methods;
or at the very least, lose faith in Amanda.

00:56:00.040 --> 00:56:04.110
The entire operation he had built was founded
on the idea that Amanda had been the first

00:56:04.110 --> 00:56:08.000
one to be rehabilitated, the prime example
of how suffering can cause a person to be

00:56:08.000 --> 00:56:09.980
reborn and lead a better life.

00:56:09.980 --> 00:56:14.290
He considered Amanda to be the closest person
to truly understanding him, so he would probably

00:56:14.290 --> 00:56:18.870
be quite defeated if she were to fail her
final test now, after two years of training.

00:56:18.870 --> 00:56:22.820
To make matters worse, she seemed to be developing
a rivalry with the other known prospective

00:56:22.820 --> 00:56:25.460
candidate to continue John’s work: Detective
Hoffman.

00:56:25.460 --> 00:56:29.450
Hoffman’s training with John was also ongoing,
and John did his best with the limited time

00:56:29.450 --> 00:56:33.070
he had to teach Hoffman to walk the fine line
that Jigsaw is supposed to walk.

00:56:33.070 --> 00:56:36.910
He must respect the lives of those test subjects
he captured, but also prepare to see them

00:56:36.910 --> 00:56:39.850
suffer in order to achieve retribution for
their sins.

00:56:39.850 --> 00:56:43.200
The day these games were held was April 28,
2006.

00:56:43.200 --> 00:56:46.990
Before the fun begins, John’s ex-wife shows
up to the Meat Packing Plant to try to plead

00:56:46.990 --> 00:56:48.980
with him and get him to stop his work.

00:56:48.980 --> 00:56:52.040
Instead of listening to her, he gives her
the key to the box left to her in his will,

00:56:52.040 --> 00:56:54.660
and tells her she will know what to do with
it when the time comes.

00:56:54.660 --> 00:56:58.600
With that, John feels he’s done everything
he can do, and asks Amanda to take him to

00:56:58.600 --> 00:56:59.600
his deathbed.

00:56:59.600 --> 00:57:04.140
His final game was about to begin, and his
assistants went to retrieve the players, Dr.

00:57:04.140 --> 00:57:06.310
Lynn Denlon and the mourning father Jeff Denlon.

00:57:06.310 --> 00:57:09.930
Hoffman got done capturing Jeff and placing
him at the start of his trial moments before

00:57:09.930 --> 00:57:14.120
Amanda got back with Lynn, and he used this
time to have one last meeting with John.

00:57:14.120 --> 00:57:17.630
It turns out that Hoffman shared the same
concerns about Amanda letting her emotions

00:57:17.630 --> 00:57:20.950
get in the way of giving her victims a fair
chance to survive.

00:57:20.950 --> 00:57:24.700
John rewards Hoffman for his honest work so
far by giving him a protection that Amanda

00:57:24.700 --> 00:57:26.480
does not have: anonymity.

00:57:26.480 --> 00:57:30.380
Amanda was already a known accomplice to Jigsaw
-- the police and FBI would have figured that

00:57:30.380 --> 00:57:33.970
out when they saw her help Daniel Matthews
out of the Nerve Gas House, since Daniel ended

00:57:33.970 --> 00:57:35.900
up being stowed in Jigsaw’s workshop.

00:57:35.900 --> 00:57:39.790
The FBI did suspect there was another accomplice,
but did not know with certainty that it was

00:57:39.790 --> 00:57:40.790
Hoffman.

00:57:40.790 --> 00:57:43.700
So John’s willingness to keep Hoffman’s
involvement a secret showed that he had more

00:57:43.700 --> 00:57:45.650
faith in Hoffman than he had in Amanda.

00:57:45.650 --> 00:57:49.680
In exchange for keeping this anonymity, he
does ask Hoffman to carry out one more task

00:57:49.680 --> 00:57:54.840
and hands him a file with instructions on
a future game which would test Ashley Kuzon, Charles Salomon,

00:57:54.840 --> 00:57:59.980
Britt Stevenson, Scott Mallick and Luba Gibbs, who all played some
part in causing and covering up a deadly fire.

00:57:59.980 --> 00:58:02.410
*Jigsaw hands over the file*
Hoffman: “What’s this?”

00:58:02.410 --> 00:58:04.300
JIGSAW: “It’s time to play a game.”

00:58:04.300 --> 00:58:08.270
Those would be the final words John said to
his longest tenured student, who slipped out

00:58:08.270 --> 00:58:11.890
a secret door before heading over to the room
where the final trial of Daniel Rigg would

00:58:11.890 --> 00:58:13.080
take place.

00:58:13.080 --> 00:58:16.990
Moments later, Amanda arrived with Lynn Denlon,
so their own game was about to begin.

00:58:16.990 --> 00:58:18.890
“Hello Dr. Denlon.”

00:58:18.890 --> 00:58:21.980
John explains that he was once her patient,
and blames her for telling him he’s going

00:58:21.980 --> 00:58:24.310
to die in such a cold clinical tone of voice.

00:58:24.310 --> 00:58:28.230
He claims that she is dead on the inside after
leaving her husband and neglecting her daughter.

00:58:28.230 --> 00:58:31.310
But when John delivers his second most used
phrase from his list of 10 Top Phrases…

00:58:31.310 --> 00:58:32.929
“What do I want?

00:58:33.610 --> 00:58:34.910
I want to play a game.”

00:58:34.910 --> 00:58:39.650
...he’s actually looking at Amanda, signifying
that this is her test as much as is it Dr.

00:58:39.650 --> 00:58:40.650
Denlon’s.

00:58:40.650 --> 00:58:43.300
This would be her final chance to prove she
can let a game play out fairly without her

00:58:43.300 --> 00:58:46.050
desire for revenge and bloodthirst getting
in the way.

00:58:46.050 --> 00:58:49.820
I mean, obviously there’s nothing fair about
any of Jigsaw’s games… but you get what

00:58:49.820 --> 00:58:50.820
I mean.

00:58:50.820 --> 00:58:54.320
When John states the rules, he simply says
he is testing her will to keep someone alive,

00:58:54.320 --> 00:58:56.650
which could apply to both Lynn and Amanda.

00:58:56.650 --> 00:59:00.340
Lynn is required to keep John alive, and Amanda
is required to keep Lynn alive.

00:59:00.340 --> 00:59:05.010
If John dies, his heart rate monitor will
stop, causing Lynn’s shotgun collar to shoot her in the head;

00:59:05.010 --> 00:59:08.650
whereas if Lynn dies, Jeff will come through
the door at the end of his trial and get revenge

00:59:08.650 --> 00:59:10.560
on the first person he sees: Amanda.

00:59:10.560 --> 00:59:12.080
The theme of the game is forgiveness.

00:59:12.080 --> 00:59:15.650
Can a father forgive the people involved in
the premature death of his son?

00:59:15.650 --> 00:59:19.080
Can Amanda forgive the victims who had faltered
in life as she once had?

00:59:19.080 --> 00:59:22.980
And can Lynn Denlon forgive the man responsible
for the kidnapping of her entire family by

00:59:22.980 --> 00:59:26.290
doing her best to keep him alive as long as
possible?

00:59:26.290 --> 00:59:29.800
As usual with Jigsaw, each of these people
were pieces of his puzzle, and they would

00:59:29.800 --> 00:59:31.700
all interlock together at the end.

00:59:31.700 --> 00:59:35.040
His confidence that each of them will end
coming together is another example of his

00:59:35.040 --> 00:59:37.710
mastery of GAME THEORY.

00:59:37.710 --> 00:59:41.310
Amanda would keep tabs on Jeff’s progress
as Dr. Denlon began to treat John.

00:59:41.310 --> 00:59:44.920
She believes John’s brain is herniating,
and suggests that they take him to a hospital,

00:59:44.920 --> 00:59:49.050
and John watches helplessly as Amanda loses
her cool and goes off on the doctor, basically

00:59:49.050 --> 00:59:51.960
telling her she needs to perform an operation
in this room.

00:59:51.960 --> 00:59:55.440
Normally, Jigsaw would not really interfere
with anything that might change the result

00:59:55.440 --> 00:59:58.050
of his games, but in this instance, he snaps
at Amanda.

00:59:58.050 --> 01:00:01.570
I think that's because she was the only one
that had seemingly recovered from her addictions,

01:00:01.570 --> 01:00:05.300
she was the only ray of hope that could make
John believe that his treatment methods actually

01:00:05.300 --> 01:00:08.780
worked, so he desperately wanted her to pass
her test so that he could die thinking that

01:00:08.780 --> 01:00:11.270
he actually had been helping his test subjects
all along.

01:00:11.270 --> 01:00:14.040
Of course, John was completely delusional
at this point.

01:00:14.040 --> 01:00:17.630
He hadn’t actually helped out anybody other
than himself, and would soon show much more

01:00:17.630 --> 01:00:20.450
quantifiable signs of his deteriorating sanity.

01:00:20.450 --> 01:00:23.860
But his sanity wasn’t the only thing that
had slipped, because moments later he would

01:00:23.860 --> 01:00:26.313
go into a life-threatening myoclonic episode.

01:00:33.270 --> 01:00:36.700
John must have been very aware that he was
getting close to the end of his life, because

01:00:36.700 --> 01:00:40.330
it was very shortly after bringing Lynn Denlon
into the picture that he convulsed into a

01:00:40.330 --> 01:00:44.350
dangerous state that required the combined
efforts of Dr. Denlon and Amanda to get the

01:00:44.350 --> 01:00:47.420
oxygen flowing back to his brain and save
his life.

01:00:47.420 --> 01:00:51.510
John was left very weak after this, but refused
to let that stop him from continuing to work

01:00:51.510 --> 01:00:52.510
on his legacy.

01:00:52.510 --> 01:00:54.710
He may have been crazy, but I gotta admire
this work ethic.

01:00:54.710 --> 01:00:57.160
Just like you should admire my work ethic
to get you to buy this merch.

01:00:57.160 --> 01:00:58.870
You can click in the link in the--

01:00:58.870 --> 01:01:02.440
I think it was while Lynn and Amanda were
out arguing in the next room when Jigsaw recorded

01:01:02.440 --> 01:01:04.990
the tape for Detective Hoffman to find after
his death.

01:01:04.990 --> 01:01:08.600
Of course, he couldn’t guarantee that Hoffman
would be the only one to hear it, so he had

01:01:08.600 --> 01:01:12.450
to speak in very general terms, not revealing
the fact that they were actually working together.

01:01:12.450 --> 01:01:14.380
“Are you there Detective?

01:01:14.380 --> 01:01:18.130
If so, you are probably the last man standing.

01:01:18.130 --> 01:01:23.510
Now perhaps you will succeed where the others
have failed.

01:01:23.510 --> 01:01:26.340
You think you will walk away untested?

01:01:26.340 --> 01:01:31.460
I promise that my work will continue.”

01:01:31.460 --> 01:01:35.070
John placed this tape next to his bed, and
as Lynn prepared for the next operation, Amanda

01:01:35.070 --> 01:01:38.640
came in to inform him that Jeff had passed
through the first room of his trial.

01:01:38.640 --> 01:01:41.770
John let Amanda know about an envelope that
he had Hoffman hide in his desk.

01:01:41.770 --> 01:01:45.310
We never find out what this note was supposed
to say, it was most likely supposed to offer

01:01:45.310 --> 01:01:48.600
Amanda some strength in words, but Hoffman
switched out the message.

01:01:48.600 --> 01:01:51.630
If you want to know more about that, you can
watch the Hoffman and Amanda Horror History

01:01:51.630 --> 01:01:52.630
episodes.

01:01:52.630 --> 01:01:56.160
When he sees Amanda becoming overwhelmed with
emotion, he once again intervenes to try to

01:01:56.160 --> 01:01:57.370
get her back on the right path.

01:01:58.298 --> 01:02:00.100
“I can’t do this.”

01:02:00.100 --> 01:02:01.255
JIGSAW: “Amanda!

01:02:01.600 --> 01:02:03.714
You can.

01:02:03.714 --> 01:02:06.071
You’re stronger now.

01:02:06.071 --> 01:02:10.940
This is another example of his blind ambition
to prove that his rehabilitation process works,

01:02:10.940 --> 01:02:13.710
despite all evidence pointing to the fact
that it doesn’t.

01:02:13.710 --> 01:02:18.080
The American Psychiatric Association notes
that psychotic behavior can include an over-inflated

01:02:18.080 --> 01:02:19.860
self image and extreme cockiness.

01:02:19.860 --> 01:02:23.410
It seems that John has reached that stage,
and he can’t accept that he was wrong about

01:02:23.410 --> 01:02:26.950
something, especially after spending the last
three years holding these games with the intention

01:02:26.950 --> 01:02:30.480
of proving that his test-subjects were missing
something, and that torturing them in his

01:02:30.480 --> 01:02:32.200
traps would help them find it.

01:02:32.200 --> 01:02:35.980
After Amanda watches Jeff complete the next
room, she reports back to John, who is surprised

01:02:35.980 --> 01:02:39.550
at the rate he is progressing, but despite
his quick advancement, the outcome of the

01:02:39.550 --> 01:02:42.430
game would depend entirely on what was about
to happen next.

01:02:42.430 --> 01:02:45.523
John gets a haircut, something that I could
use right about now.

01:02:45.709 --> 01:02:46.884
ONE PANDEMIC LATER: If only you knew.......

01:02:46.884 --> 01:02:50.110
in preparation of the brain surgery that Lynn was about to perform.

01:02:50.110 --> 01:02:53.190
This would prevent the brain from pushing
up against John’s skull and theoretically

01:02:53.190 --> 01:02:55.190
reduce his headaches and improve his motor
skills.

01:02:55.190 --> 01:02:59.770
While it was possible to use numbing agents,
John had to be awake and alert for this procedure,

01:02:59.770 --> 01:03:03.200
which involved Dr. Denlon drilling into his
skull and cutting open a window using this

01:03:03.200 --> 01:03:04.330
little sawblade.

01:03:04.330 --> 01:03:05.330
Get it?

01:03:05.330 --> 01:03:06.330
Cause Saw?

01:03:06.330 --> 01:03:08.510
That’s the name of the franchise…

01:03:08.510 --> 01:03:10.390
“Ha, ha.

01:03:10.390 --> 01:03:11.390
Ha…”

01:03:11.390 --> 01:03:14.530
Something about this procedure triggers some
memories in his brain of a picnic he went

01:03:14.530 --> 01:03:17.390
on when he was married to Jill, which he had
recorded on his camcorder.

01:03:17.390 --> 01:03:21.201
I’m sure that tape is right there on the
shelf at home next to all his other home videos.

01:03:21.334 --> 01:03:24.079
JIGSAW: "More comfortable in chains than you are in freedom."

01:03:24.079 --> 01:03:27.860
During the hallucination, John tries to tell
his wife “I love you,” but that causes

01:03:27.860 --> 01:03:32.300
it to look like he’s telling Lynn Denlon
he loves her, making Amanda get super jealous

01:03:32.300 --> 01:03:33.501
and causing her to storm out.

01:03:33.501 --> 01:03:39.180
“Just get out of here you stupid dumb animal.”

01:03:39.180 --> 01:03:43.150
Once again, Dr. Denlon’s efforts are able
to buy John a little more time, and it seems

01:03:43.150 --> 01:03:46.080
as if she’s actually starting to change
her attitude, for example we see her put her

01:03:46.080 --> 01:03:49.800
wedding ring back on as if to suggest that
seeing John fighting for more time made her

01:03:49.800 --> 01:03:51.780
appreciate her time with her husband.

01:03:51.780 --> 01:03:56.290
Amanda is still in jealous girlfriend mode,
a very serious mental disease that I discussed

01:03:56.290 --> 01:04:00.200
in great detail in her own Horror History
episode, and she comes in and starts kissing

01:04:00.200 --> 01:04:01.390
John’s face and neck.

01:04:01.390 --> 01:04:04.790
Lynn tells her that John is passed out and
he can’t hear her, and again, Amanda’s

01:04:04.790 --> 01:04:07.170
temper flares up and she threatens to kill
Lynn.

01:04:07.170 --> 01:04:12.490
Once again, Jigsaw has to intervene and scold
her… wait a minute John, weren’t you just

01:04:12.490 --> 01:04:13.490
asleep?

01:04:13.490 --> 01:04:17.520
So you mean to tell me you just gained consciousness
and had a full understanding of what was going

01:04:17.520 --> 01:04:21.080
on in the two seconds between when this happened
and when this happened?

01:04:21.080 --> 01:04:25.640
And you were totally passed out and not pretending
to be asleep when Amanda was all over you

01:04:25.640 --> 01:04:26.640
right here?

01:04:26.640 --> 01:04:27.680
I see you John Kramer.

01:04:27.680 --> 01:04:29.830
I SEE YOU!

01:04:29.830 --> 01:04:33.140
Meanwhile Jeff continues on through his trial,
eventually making it to the room where he

01:04:33.140 --> 01:04:36.870
has the opportunity to save his son’s killer
from what John considers to be his personal

01:04:36.870 --> 01:04:38.360
favorite trap: The Rack.

01:04:38.360 --> 01:04:43.050
The fact that John even has a favorite torture
device is proof that he had developed a psychological

01:04:43.050 --> 01:04:46.650
dependence on the feeling he got from hurting
others and that this was no longer solely

01:04:46.650 --> 01:04:48.010
about curing people.

01:04:48.010 --> 01:04:52.300
The trap is also a modern day crucifix, which
adds credence to his God-complex and development

01:04:52.300 --> 01:04:53.970
of his teachings as a religion.

01:04:53.970 --> 01:04:57.420
Back in the operation room, John asks Lynn
to talk about her husband, causing Lynn to

01:04:57.420 --> 01:05:00.260
defend her marriage against him, which is
essentially what he wants.

01:05:00.260 --> 01:05:02.810
He wants her to get passionate and take back
her life.

01:05:02.810 --> 01:05:07.110
She begs for him to let her go free and right
as he takes her hand, Amanda walks in, causing

01:05:07.110 --> 01:05:08.800
more jealous rage.

01:05:08.800 --> 01:05:09.910
John sends her off…

01:05:09.910 --> 01:05:11.330
“We’re fine Amanda.

01:05:11.330 --> 01:05:13.220
We don’t need you.”

01:05:13.220 --> 01:05:17.980
It does seem a little… counter-productive....
for Jigsaw to do something to piss off Amanda

01:05:17.980 --> 01:05:20.400
like this when he really wants her to pass
her test.

01:05:20.400 --> 01:05:23.580
It could be that he knew that she would have
to endure some emotional turmoil in order

01:05:23.580 --> 01:05:27.290
to prove that she’s be able to handle her
emotions when he’s no longer around, but

01:05:27.290 --> 01:05:30.290
I don’t think he was really in the mind
frame of giving his victims “proper” tests

01:05:30.290 --> 01:05:31.290
at this point.

01:05:31.290 --> 01:05:34.300
I think more what was going on is he sensed
he was close to a breakthrough with Lynn,

01:05:34.300 --> 01:05:36.280
and didn’t want Amanda to interrupt it.

01:05:36.280 --> 01:05:39.021
Why settle for one successful patient when
he could possibly have two?

01:05:39.021 --> 01:05:42.070
“If you make it through this Lynn, you’re
going to thank me one day, just as Amanda

01:05:42.070 --> 01:05:43.650
did.”

01:05:43.650 --> 01:05:47.470
As he continued to talk with Lynn, he knew
that it would not be long before Amanda announced

01:05:47.470 --> 01:05:51.050
that Jeff had passed through the final room
and would soon be headed to the operation

01:05:51.050 --> 01:05:52.050
room.

01:05:52.050 --> 01:05:54.910
With this, came the possibility that Jeff
would try to get revenge on his captor, so

01:05:54.910 --> 01:05:59.250
it was time for John to hide the tape that
he had previously recorded for Detective Hoffman.

01:05:59.250 --> 01:06:03.070
Since Amanda’s safety was also not guaranteed,
he covered the tape in a protective coat of

01:06:03.070 --> 01:06:07.070
candle wax and swallowed it, so that the medical
examiners would find it in his stomach and

01:06:07.070 --> 01:06:09.070
forward it to Detective Hoffman.

01:06:09.070 --> 01:06:11.450
Sometimes when people know they are going
to die they get to have their favorite food

01:06:11.450 --> 01:06:12.530
as a final meal.

01:06:12.530 --> 01:06:14.930
John gets to have an audio tape covered in
wax.

01:06:14.930 --> 01:06:15.930
So….

01:06:15.930 --> 01:06:20.120
“The less we eats, the mores less fats we
get at ourselves.”

01:06:20.120 --> 01:06:23.450
Not long after, Amanda would come into the
room to deliver the message that Jeff had

01:06:23.450 --> 01:06:25.100
completed his final test.

01:06:25.100 --> 01:06:29.230
This meant that Lynn had kept John alive long
enough to pass her test, and he orders Amanda

01:06:29.230 --> 01:06:30.470
to let her go free.

01:06:30.470 --> 01:06:33.314
Only Amanda has… other ideas…

01:06:33.314 --> 01:06:34.794
“I said no.”

01:06:46.070 --> 01:06:50.340
The Jeff Denlon Trials, as with the Barn Game,
The Bathroom Game and The Nerve Gas House

01:06:50.340 --> 01:06:54.180
Game before it, end when the pieces of the
puzzle, the people involved with those being

01:06:54.180 --> 01:06:58.820
tested come together; and as with The Bathroom
Game, this time they all literally come together

01:06:58.820 --> 01:07:00.110
in the same room.

01:07:00.110 --> 01:07:03.720
Amanda’s temper and jealousy had once again
gotten the better of her, and she refuses

01:07:03.720 --> 01:07:06.390
to let Lynn go free after passing her test.

01:07:06.390 --> 01:07:10.050
John knows he cannot directly say what will
happen if Amanda kills Lynn, but he does give

01:07:10.050 --> 01:07:13.960
the warning that Lynn’s life is important,
because she controls the outcome of Amanda’s

01:07:13.960 --> 01:07:14.960
life.

01:07:14.960 --> 01:07:18.760
That ends up making Amanda even more upset,
and John tries to justify it by bringing up

01:07:18.760 --> 01:07:22.300
the victims that Amanda had murdered, how
he had cleaned up her mistakes and forgiven

01:07:22.300 --> 01:07:24.980
her, but how he will not allow her to go on
as a murderer.

01:07:24.980 --> 01:07:29.450
Amanda argues that Lynn could not have rehabilitated,
because nobody they had tested ever really

01:07:29.450 --> 01:07:30.450
changed.

01:07:30.450 --> 01:07:33.220
She proceeds to shoot Lynn Denlon, and when
she does, Jeff is there to see it.

01:07:33.220 --> 01:07:36.000
In retaliation, Jeff fires back and kills
Amanda.

01:07:36.000 --> 01:07:39.460
With Lynn dying on the floor, Jigsaw has one
final final test for Jeff.

01:07:39.460 --> 01:07:42.950
The lesson he had been trying to teach throughout
this entire endeavor was to forgive.

01:07:42.950 --> 01:07:47.040
While Jeff had shown signs of forgiveness
in each stage of his trial, he was unable

01:07:47.040 --> 01:07:50.910
to save any of the people involved in the
accident that resulted in his son’s death.

01:07:50.910 --> 01:07:55.480
Now we would be faced with one more decision,
to exact his revenge on the man responsible

01:07:55.480 --> 01:07:59.600
for putting him and his wife through even
more hell, or to let Jigsaw live in exchange

01:07:59.600 --> 01:08:01.730
for a chance to save Lynn’s life.

01:08:01.730 --> 01:08:05.320
After much deliberation, Jeff makes his choice.

01:08:05.320 --> 01:08:07.090
“I forgive you…”

01:08:07.090 --> 01:08:10.050
But in this case… forgiveness is not enough.

01:08:10.050 --> 01:08:15.040
Even John, in the face of death, cannot help
but smile when Jeff fires up the circular

01:08:15.040 --> 01:08:16.040
saw blade.

01:08:16.040 --> 01:08:18.769
I think the irony of this twist was not lost
on him.

01:08:18.769 --> 01:08:23.049
After all people who he had made suffer, it
would be one of his most tortured test-subjects

01:08:23.049 --> 01:08:25.520
who would reverse that suffering back onto
him

01:08:25.520 --> 01:08:29.699
And with a circular spinning Saw blade no
less, the very same type of weapon he used

01:08:29.699 --> 01:08:33.380
upon his victims in the very first portion
of his first game at the barn.

01:08:33.380 --> 01:08:37.029
It’s almost like that baseball game I brought
up earlier, where Aroldis Chapman gave up

01:08:37.029 --> 01:08:41.409
the ALCS clinching home run, and all he can
do is give this weird smile, because he knew

01:08:41.409 --> 01:08:43.989
that Altuve waiting on an off speed pitch
was no coincidence.

01:08:44.989 --> 01:08:47.819
With his very last bit of life John rolls
Jeff’s tape.

01:08:47.819 --> 01:08:49.623
“Hello Jeff.

01:08:49.623 --> 01:08:54.415
I made this tape as an insurance policy if
you will.

01:08:54.415 --> 01:09:00.159
… I was your final test of forgiveness and
if you are listening to this then you failed.

01:09:00.159 --> 01:09:02.529
Now you must pay the price.”

01:09:02.529 --> 01:09:06.509
The tape reveals that Jeff’s other child,
Corbett, is locked away somewhere and only

01:09:06.509 --> 01:09:08.040
John knows the location.

01:09:08.040 --> 01:09:11.900
By killing Jigsaw, Jeff had essentially locked
the tomb of his own daughter.

01:09:11.900 --> 01:09:15.650
Even if John had lived, there is no excuse
he could have made to his followers for trapping

01:09:15.650 --> 01:09:17.949
an innocent young girl just to punish Jeff.

01:09:17.949 --> 01:09:22.981
So on the evening of April 28th, 2006, John’s
heart rate monitor flatlines, and the man

01:09:22.981 --> 01:09:26.829
feared by an entire city as the Jigsaw killer
is no more.

01:09:26.829 --> 01:09:31.349
With his death, Lynn’s collar goes off and
Jeff is locked inside the operation room for

01:09:31.349 --> 01:09:32.349
life.

01:09:32.349 --> 01:09:36.369
After years of insistence that his methods
worked, John died knowing that he had failed.

01:09:36.369 --> 01:09:40.569
In early May, they would perform the autopsy
on John’s body and inside of his stomach

01:09:40.569 --> 01:09:44.339
they found, not only John’s cocoa puffs,
but also the tape left for Detective Hoffman

01:09:44.339 --> 01:09:47.480
who would continue to fill the shoes of Jigsaw
until March of 2007.

01:09:47.480 --> 01:09:51.499
John’s body was buried in a local cemetery,
where it would remain until the year 2016,

01:09:51.499 --> 01:09:55.660
when his first disciple, Logan Nelson, dug
up his casket and switched his body with that

01:09:55.660 --> 01:09:56.660
of Edgar Munsen.

01:09:56.660 --> 01:09:59.690
It is unknown where Kramer’s body currently
resides.

01:09:59.690 --> 01:10:02.739
Throughout this video, we have discovered
the different puzzle pieces that make up the

01:10:02.739 --> 01:10:04.249
life of John Kramer.

01:10:04.249 --> 01:10:08.219
Just as he played games with his victims,
his own life, in a way, was a game where each

01:10:08.219 --> 01:10:12.090
of these pieces came together to form an icon
named Jigsaw.

01:10:12.090 --> 01:10:16.310
After a life of his own agony, he gave himself
the power to judge the lives of others, and

01:10:16.310 --> 01:10:19.150
as a result developed a dependence on human
suffering.

01:10:19.150 --> 01:10:23.059
This caused him to become a psychopath, the
likes of which rival the greatest serial killers

01:10:23.059 --> 01:10:24.090
in all of fiction.

01:10:24.090 --> 01:10:27.869
He developed a God-complex, and transformed
his work from a series of acts of violence

01:10:27.869 --> 01:10:32.309
into a movement: a religion with its own symbols,
code of conduct and followers.

01:10:32.309 --> 01:10:36.130
He claimed to offer all of his subjects a
second chance at life, but in reality, he

01:10:36.130 --> 01:10:39.909
destroyed the lives of over 50 people, some
of which were bad criminals and some of which

01:10:39.909 --> 01:10:41.530
were completely innocent.

01:10:41.530 --> 01:10:44.930
He was able to get as far as he did based
on two things he did very well.

01:10:44.930 --> 01:10:48.929
The first was his engineering degree, he was
a mechanical mastermind, making his traps

01:10:48.929 --> 01:10:52.400
perfect machines that were only escapable
in ways that he intended.

01:10:52.400 --> 01:10:56.829
The second was his ability to anticipate the
human mind, he was a master of game theory,

01:10:56.829 --> 01:11:00.570
so every conceivable possibility for each
game, and really for anything he did in life

01:11:00.570 --> 01:11:03.050
was already thought out and had a solution.

01:11:03.050 --> 01:11:04.900
And what does that leave us with?

01:11:04.900 --> 01:11:07.730
An almost finished puzzle.

01:11:07.730 --> 01:11:11.539
Because with all of John’s intellect and
ability, he was never any better than any

01:11:11.539 --> 01:11:12.712
of the people he tested.

01:11:12.712 --> 01:11:15.689
Jigsaw was missing a vital piece.

01:11:19.835 --> 01:11:24.269
If you’re a fan of Saw, click the playlist
on the left to see my Horror History analysis’

01:11:24.269 --> 01:11:26.050
of other Saw characters.

01:11:26.050 --> 01:11:30.559
And if you love horror, make sure you subscribe
to CZsWorld for new horrors every week, ring

01:11:30.559 --> 01:11:34.849
the deathbell for notifications and I’ll
see you in the next one.

01:11:34.849 --> 01:11:36.940
Assuming we both survive.

